atus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree - that is my worry as well.<br /> <br /> Edit: <a href=\"https://www.twitch.tv/worldofdarkness\" target=\"_blank\">Achilli and Outstar discuss the book and clans in today's (11/12/2020) twitch stream.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 11-12-2020, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T19:35:00-08:00","id":1423443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1423397#post1423397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.renegadegamestudios.com/vampire-the-masquerade-rivals-expandable-card-game\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://cdn11.bigcommerce.com/s-kftzvkkgjv/products/121/images/558/Vampire3Dsquare__06712.1639072510.386.513.png?c=1\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.renegadegamestudios.com/vampire-the-masquerade-rivals-expandable-card-game\" target=\"_blank\"> Vampire: The Masquerade Rivals Expandable Card Game </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.renegadegamestudios.com/vampire-the-masquerade-rivals-expandable-card-game\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.renegadegamestudios.com/vampire-the-masquerade-rivals-expandable-card-game </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Renegade Games Online Store </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> They seem to be the company behind the VtM card game. Creative direction will be decided by World of Darkness (which means Paradox, I guess?) and Justin Achilli and I trust Justin Achilli to do good with WoD development.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In the video Jason stated they will develop and publish everything the WoD team considers outside of the core. Renegade has developed one ttrpg on their own that I can find, and from what I can tell published other ttrpgs (Alice is Missing, Kids on Bike/Brooms, Outbreak) that were developed by Hunters Entertainment (the company that <i>was </i>developing WtA 5)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T19:52:04-08:00","id":1423449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1423412#post1423412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can't imagine why they're less concerned about those guys these days.<br /> <br /> BTW, wasn't the officiate at the Vermillion Wedding Serena the White?</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost certainly yes. She's identified as 'Serenna of the al-Amin' and al-Amin is the name of the Islamic Salubri.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1423423#post1423423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heart of the Forest said that about 90% of werewolves died in the Apocalypse but they avoided it. Only the very old and the very young survived.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously? How can you have a devastating Apocalypse that <u><i><b>NINETY PERCENT</b></i></u>of the Garou population but leaves the world just fine? Or are they just putting WtA in a post-apocalyptic setting?<br /> <br /> Like say what you want about the Beckoning, the Second Inquisition and all that but at least it's something that makes sense as something that would affect the world of Kindred without radically affecting the rest of the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Suddenly I'm having greater fears for the rest of WoD in the Fifth Edition...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1423437#post1423437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree - that is my worry as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I third this. While I came into VtM and WoD during the Rev Ed, having since widened my view of WoD through the earlier editions and x20 Edition, making the flaws of the Rev Ed more apparent since my early days. While I do like the idea of the Seven, I don't think they work too well for PCs for most players. V20's approach to the Salubri was a solid way to present the Bloodline for both NPCs and PCs.<br /> <br /> And with the Camarilla-Ashirra Alliance there is an opportunity to take what LotB set up and bring the Salubri back into the open as the Ashirra had been protecting the Islamic Salubri and I doubt they would cease to do that with their alliance. But they could have also requested that as part of the alliance, the pogroms against the Salubri cease at least within the Cam. The Seven can still be around and be viewed by everyone else with a mixture of fear and reverence while there are other Salubri doing their own things. And for that matter, it also provides the chance for a reunification between the three Castes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: <a href=\"https://www.twitch.tv/worldofdarkness\" target=\"_blank\">Achilli and Outstar discuss the book and clans in today's (11/12/2020) twitch stream.</a> </div> </div> </div>Anyone got the keynotes of the stream?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T20:35:04-08:00","id":1423458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Seriously? How can you have a devastating Apocalypse that <u><i><b>NINETY PERCENT</b></i></u>of the Garou population but leaves the world just fine? Or are they just putting WtA in a post-apocalyptic setting? </div> </div> </div>Apparently almost all of the Garou went into the Umbra to stop the Apocalypse and they didn't come back.<br /> <br /> But Gaia didn't end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T21:09:02-08:00","id":1423463,"title":"","content":"Bruh I really hope that's just the game doing video game stuff and not anything to do with the TTRP. Anyways with WoD itself finally back in saddle I doubt any of the stuff planned for other &quot;5&quot; lines will come to fruition. Different Tales that made Heart of the Forest; do they have any connections with the development of the TTRP in the first place?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 11-13-2020, 03:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T22:19:27-08:00","id":1423471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1423458#post1423458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Apparently almost all of the Garou went into the Umbra to stop the Apocalypse and they didn't come back.<br /> <br /> But Gaia didn't end.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Okay that just sounds really lame and pointless. It sounds like they're doing for W5 what they did for V5, removing the big leaders so younger ones could take their place while forgetting one very important thing, Garou are mortal. More than that, their very nature is that they die in battle, that they don't die of old age. That some of the major characters die in the span of time between the 90s and 2020s is to be expected.<br /> <br /> Nor does WtA need it's world to be worse by having a mass die-off of Garou. The environmental problems are still there and not going away any time soon. In fact IRL, the signs point to things getting worse. So why bother with a pointless non-apocalypse Apocalypse?<br /> <br /> I say that as someone who's not the biggest WtA fan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T22:25:13-08:00","id":1423473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1423458#post1423458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Apparently almost all of the Garou went into the Umbra to stop the Apocalypse and they didn't come back.<br /> <br /> But Gaia didn't end.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So why even bother with W5?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Hecata are a sect not a clan.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24211-frontline989","name":"Frontline989","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-13T02:15:36-08:00","id":1423496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1423423#post1423423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heart of the Forest said that about 90% of werewolves died in the Apocalypse but they avoided it. Only the very old and the very young survived.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I can remember there are in character quotes from the NPCs in that game stating that &quot;A LOT OF GAROUS DIED IN THE NINETIES&quot;. I don't know where you found the 90% figure.<br /> <br /> What's likely (IMO) is W5 will do the same V5 did: keep some of the major stuff that happened in the Apocalypse book without bringing the Apocalypse to fruition (V5 did keep most of what happened before Gehenna and in the book itself but did not wipe out the get of Caine as a whole, obviously). I think people like Jonas Albrecht, Yuri Konietzko and Zhyzhak are dead and gone though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-13T03:21:48-08:00","id":1423505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frontline989</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1423473#post1423473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So why even bother with W5?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because its been decades and the Garou Nation is rebuilding? All those dead werewolves are reincarnating after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1423463#post1423463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bruh I really hope that's just the game doing video game stuff and not anything to do with the TTRP. Anyways with WoD itself finally back in saddle I doubt any of the stuff planned for other &quot;5&quot; lines will come to fruition. Different Tales that made Heart of the Forest; do they have any connections with the development of the TTRP in the first place?</div> </div> </div> </div>They've said that they worked heavily with the W5 development team.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-13T06:51:24-08:00","id":1423542,"title":"","content":"With Modiphius no longer being involved in the gameline, I imagine that White Wolf/Paradox is going to have to reprint the Modiphius books under their new banner with the errata that they've complied (some of which is being included in the Companion per the most recent interview with Justin Achilli). I'd personally like to see the Player's Guide deliver on the promise of all Clans in one location and then a Storyteller's Guide include the Mortal and Ghouls rules, the collected Loresheets, and then some of the fluff found in Camarilla, Anarch, and Sabbat. <br /> <br /> Does anyone else have thoughts on these theoretical &quot;revised&quot; books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25976-differentjustin","name":"DifferentJustin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-13T08:21:22-08:00","id":1423560,"title":"","content":"When it comes to the Companion,<br /> I am hopefull that they will make a physical book next year as martyna sad that that they are looking into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":25995,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","user":"Ethryo","date":". 11-13-2020, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-13T09:08:25-08:00","id":1423569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"><