umber of Terah in Hindi</li> <li>13 is the number of Confucian Classics (I Ching, etc)</li> <li>13 is the smallest emery number, a prime number, a happy number, a Fibonacci number and is mathematically significant in a bunch of ways</li> <li>13 is the number of Archemedean solids in geometry</li> <li>The 13th day of various particular Months is considered significant across a load of religions, ancient and current.</li> <li>13 is considered lucky in some cultures and unlucky in others.</li> <li>Friday the 13th is a bad horror movie series, but is nevertheless another reference.</li> <li>13 is the number of Clans in Vampire: The Masquerade</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's the 13 GREAT clans of Caine. Maybe now one of them isn't so great. Take Gangrel. Very low energy. Not saying they're bad, just maybe they're not so great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11519-popevlad","name":"PopeVlad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T08:57:52-08:00","id":1424284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424272#post1424272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bloodlines? Sure. Love myself some african bloodlines, though Osebo seem like the most one-track murdery murder monsters of all time. Abomwe is... I dislike the concept somewhat. Indian Ventrue being Thaumaturges is great. Gangrel adopting to their land is great, So if we could get this kinda stuff in the Americas and the far east...<br /> <br /> But full blown clans? Veto.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Clans.<br /> <br /> Because there's no need to not have more than 13 Clans. Why couldn't more Antediluvians survive the Flood?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T09:53:57-08:00","id":1424294,"title":"","content":"They did. Salout never actually got killed by the Tremere. Capadcious survived as a Specter. There are arguably 15 clans pre V5. If you count the Salubri and the Cappadocians. Salout restoring his clan to their status, is pretty on point with everything revised did with Salout. <br /> <br /> As for other Antedluvians...Gehenna provides several other ones that survived the flood that didn't make clans (such as the ones in fair as foul in Gehenna. Which in my head canon made the Laibon legacies).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T10:01:53-08:00","id":1424298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424284#post1424284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, Clans.<br /> <br /> Because there's no need to not have more than 13 Clans. Why couldn't more Antediluvians survive the Flood?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cause God&gt;Antedeluvians and the survivors got lucky. <br /> Or<br /> Cause Antedeluvians chomped down on other Antedeluvians <br /> Or<br /> Cause the second generation really didn't make all that many kids. <br /> <br /> I recognize that V5 is dancing to it's own tune, but just revealing more antedeluvians with full-blown clans that should be considered equal to the other clans strikes me as bad taste and pandering. By all means, make Brujah African, Ventrue Indian, Enoia American... I don't really want to make anyone east asian because the KOTE Concept is good even if the execution needs work, but the only Ante I think is white-white is Set with his red hair and God-Of-Foreigners shtick (even then, there might have been more historical people with red hair in central asia, but that might just be a way of saying brown) But adding Lu-Pang-Hai, Houloutl and Achebe as full-blown antideluvians who've always been there with giant clans the westerners have been to ignorant to discover till now is just... How would you put that in without it seeming cheap?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T11:21:35-08:00","id":1424312,"title":"","content":"I liked theory the Drowned were the Clans that survived the Great Flood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T11:42:49-08:00","id":1424321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424294#post1424294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They did. Salout never actually got killed by the Tremere. Capadcious survived as a Specter. There are arguably 15 clans pre V5. If you count the Salubri and the Cappadocians. Salout restoring his clan to their status, is pretty on point with everything revised did with Salout.<br /> <br /> As for other Antedluvians...Gehenna provides several other ones that survived the flood that didn't make clans (such as the ones in fair as foul in Gehenna. Which in my head canon made the Laibon legacies).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Part of the backstory of the game is how the Tremere and Giovanni wiped out the Salubri and Cappadocians - with any of the scattered remnants relegated to bing a bloodline. Its also why vampires outside of the 13 Clans are referred collectively as Caitiff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, Clans.<br /> <br /> Because there's no need to not have more than 13 Clans. Why couldn't more Antediluvians survive the Flood?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the backstory of the game seeks to make the number 13 significant, then adding new Clans without any explanation just flies in the face of the game\u2019s own lore. The terms Antediluvian and Methelusah are lifted from the Hebrew Bible especially, where 13 is seen as significant in all sorts of ways. Various supernatural associations with the number 13 possibly stemmed from there, but it\u2019s actually had significance to a whole bunch of cultures, possibly because of its mathematical and astrological qualities. When the Vampire game picked up on the number 13 for the number of Clans, it was a Biblical reference, and it adds to the atmosphere of the setting. The answers here - just handwaving it away when it\u2019s been canon in the game since 1991 - just seem really cavalier to me.<br /> <br /> Whether or not it is a serious issue could be seen as an individual thing, but as a marker of a possible new direction of the game under a new development team, actually, I think I object to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 11-16-2020, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T12:25:42-08:00","id":1424328,"title":"","content":"Ya and then they printed the Harbingers of Skulls and Salubri Antitbiru for example. Making them more numerous then previously. Such as the old argument of &quot;there's only 7 Salubri left!&quot; then they made a lot of supplement books that proved that wasn't the case...like at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T12:32:12-08:00","id":1424330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424328#post1424328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ya and then they printed the Harbingers of Skulls and Salubri Antitbiru for example. Making them more numerous then previously. Such as the old argument of &quot;there's only 7 Salubri left!&quot; then they made a lot of supplement books that proved that wasn't the case...like at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you, the old books made it clear that the Camarilla and Sabbat were acting like 3/4ths of the Earth was &quot;here be dragons.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T12:37:50-08:00","id":1424331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424272#post1424272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bloodlines? Sure. Love myself some african bloodlines, though Osebo seem like the most one-track murdery murder monsters of all time. Abomwe is... I dislike the concept somewhat. Indian Ventrue being Thaumaturges is great. Gangrel adopting to their land is great, So if we could get this kinda stuff in the Americas and the far east...<br /> <br /> But full blown clans? Veto.</div> </div> </div> </div>Non Cainite clans.......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T15:11:49-08:00","id":1424368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424330#post1424330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mind you, the old books made it clear that the Camarilla and Sabbat were acting like 3/4ths of the Earth was &quot;here be dragons.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Really? <br /> Like. <br /> Europeans conquered the world. Near all of it. The Camarilla and the Sabbat would've came with them. <br /> If anything, it's strange the Ashira are still a thing and the Laibon aren't a bygone confined to the untamed lands of central africa. The Cathayans similarly should've mostly retreated to inner/north/west china and the undeveloped parts of SE Asia. <br /> Colonialism happened, and as above, so below; When will we stop acting like foreign lands are special and mystical and reject technology and haven't been fucking globalized? Make the Camarilla the Global conspiracy it was sold as already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T16:05:28-08:00","id":1424373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424368#post1424368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really?<br /> Like.<br /> Europeans conquered the world. Near all of it. The Camarilla and the Sabbat would've came with them.<br /> If anything, it's strange the Ashira are still a thing and the Laibon aren't a bygone confined to the untamed lands of central africa. The Cathayans similarly should've mostly retreated to inner/north/west china and the undeveloped parts of SE Asia.<br /> Colonialism happened, and as above, so below; When will we stop acting like foreign lands are special and mystical and reject technology and haven't been fucking globalized? Make the Camarilla the Global conspiracy it was sold as already.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, actually.<br /> <br /> The books indicate that Europe may have taken over Africa but Kindred know nothing about the interior of the continent.<br /> <br /> Ditto China, Japan, and other places.<br /> <br /> Monster imperialism was limited by the undead.<br /> <br /> Which is funny, when you think about it. The mortals were more successful at being conquering assholes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T16:34:58-08:00","id":1424377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Europeans conquered the world. Near all of it. The Camarilla and the Sabbat would've came with them.<br /> If anything, it's strange the Ashira are still a thing and the Laibon aren't a bygone confined to the untamed lands of central africa. The Cathayans similarly should've mostly retreated to inner/north/west china and the undeveloped parts of SE Asia.<br /> Colonialism happened, and as above, so below; When will we stop acting like foreign lands are special and mystical and reject technology and haven't been fucking globalized? Make the Camarilla the Global conspiracy it was sold as already.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know the common motif in this franchise that despite all the things supernaturals do to humans in the background, they still have their agency and can do things on their own right with little to no input from the supernaturals? Just because the mortals did colonialism doesn't mean the Camarilla and Sabbat would just go gung-ho in the supernatural parallel of all things. The case where this happened was in South America really because the Kindred there (pre-V5 before the invention of the Drowned) were all Methuselahs who didn't sire childer. The Sabbat barely could beat them and had to use their numerical advantage. <br /> <br /> Now think of that on even numbers. &quot;As above, so below&quot; doesn't really mean much; Western Kindred have influence, but they only can do so much. The Camarilla never was a global conspiracy too, only really being in the Americas and Europe. The only global &quot;conspiracy&quot; you can say is the Antediluvians and Methuselahs pulling the strings of all Vampires around the world; but the former isn't even in petty Sects of modern Vampires and the latter, Methuselahs, only have minuscule numbers in either of the 3 main sects (Camarilla, Sabbat, Anarch).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T17:19:36-08:00","id":1424389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424195#post1424195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Frankly, it should be. It is a canon part of the game - and it\u2019s significant to the lore of the game. The game is based on a superstitious premise and biblical undertones. Ditching the 13 Clans motif affects the atmosphere of the game, and it should at least have some form of explanation.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing about canon is that it doesn't describe a real existing universe. It describes a fictional place that developers, writers, and editors present and can do so as they choose (assuming agreement). There's no metaphysical law of the universe that demands 13 clans, it's just a thematic element worked into the game at one point. It can be changed at any time, and should be as desired in preference to maintaining it just because it's always been that way. There's been tons of changes to canon in Vampire alone since it was first published in 1991, and there's likely to be more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424321#post1424321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really. Part of the backstory of the game is how the Tremere and Giovanni wiped out the Salubri and Cappadocians - with any of the scattered remnants relegated to bing a bloodline. Its also why vampires outside of the 13 Clans are referred collectively as Caitiff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this a change in V5? Because Caitiff have always been &quot;clanless&quot; as distinct from bloodlines and clans with their clan disciplines and weaknesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 11-16-2020, 08:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T17:22:18-08:00","id":1424390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PopeVlad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424274#post1424274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's the 13 GREAT clans of Caine. Maybe now one of them isn't so great. Take Gangrel. Very low energy. Not saying they're bad, just maybe they're not so great.</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides, the bloodline/clan distinction is linguistic, not objective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T18:21:53-08:00","id":1424403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424389#post1424389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing about canon is that it doesn't describe a real existing universe. It describes a fictional place that developers, writers, and editors present and can do so as they choose (assuming agreement). There's no metaphysical law of the universe that demands 13 clans, it's just a thematic element worked into the game at one point. It can be changed at any time, and should be as desired in preference to maintaining it just because it's always been that way. There's been tons of changes to canon in Vampire alone since it was first published in 1991, and there's likely to be more.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are atmospheric and thematic reasons why you would keep 13 Clans, as outlined above - and if there is going to be a change in something as fundamental to the setting as that ought to at least have a good explanation from the developers. By the same token, you could just decide that the Book of Nod or the Cainite backstory is no longer a thing in the game. It\u2019s not as if the game background itself always made a big thing about having 13 Clans (or 13 \u2019Tribes\u2019 as described in the Book of Nod), and it forms the basis of why the succession of Tremere/Salubri, for example, is an element in the backstory of the game. Handwaving it away, in a cavalier sense, just erodes against what has been written before and undermines the lore of the game. If there are to be more Clans, then there ought to be a reason. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is this a change in V5? Because Caitiff have always been &quot;clanless&quot; as distinct from bloodlines and clans with their clan disciplines and weaknesses. </div> </div> </div>No change. The Caitiff have always been Clanless. However, V1 also described 13 Clans/Tribes, as above, and discussed the difference between Bloodlines and Clans as a concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T18:42:47-08:00","id":1424407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424403#post1424403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are atmospheric and thematic reasons why you would keep 13 Clans, as outlined above - and if there is going to be a change in something as fundamental to the setting as that ought to at least have a good explanation from the developers. By the same token, you could just decide that the Book of Nod or the Cainite backstory is no longer a thing in the game. It\u2019s not as if the game background itself always made a big thing about having 13 Clans (or 13 \u2019Tribes\u2019 as described in the Book of Nod), and it forms the basis of why the succession of Tremere/Salubri, for example, is an element in the backstory of the game. Handwaving it away, in a cavalier sense, just erodes against what has been written before and undermines the lore of the game. If there are to be more Clans, then there ought to be a reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason can be &quot;We decided we want more clans.&quot; It's fiction, it's made up. It's not a real thing, nor does it describe a real thing. Of course any such decision would be contextualized, but it looks like they're going to call the Salubri a clan anyway, so we're already past the triskadeka event horizon.<br /> <br /> The succession of the Tremere over the Salubri isn't because there were 13 clans, it's because the Tremere wanted the power of having a third generation founder.<br /> <br /> It doesn't erode the lore. There are a lot of things in V5 that I personally feel erodes the <i>game</i> but I do not believe any of it particularly erodes the lore. One of the things about a fictional setting is that we're always going be learning new things about the setting, we're going to learn things that recontextualize what we already know, and we're going to learn things that may contradict what we knew before. This has been the case for sure since first edition, and since 13 is just a number, it's fine if there are 14 or 15 or 16 or 12. The Book of Nod itself, like all accounts of Cainite history, isn't bound to be historically factual within the game itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424403#post1424403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No change. The Caitiff have always been Clanless. However, V1 also described 13 Clans/Tribes, as above, and discussed the difference between Bloodlines and Clans as a concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference between a bloodline and a clan is like the difference between a planet and a dwarf planet. It may not be arbitrary, but it's a semantic distinction based on features deemed to make something a planet or a dwarf planet, and such definitions could change in the future.<br /> <br /> First edition Vampire said there might only be nine antediluvians or as many as 27, so the idea that &quot;there were always 13 antediluvians&quot; isn't even accurate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T19:03:30-08:00","id":1424408,"title":"","content":"We have 14 Clans because people keep referring to the Salubri as a Clan instead of a Bloodline. The line got too blurred and they just gave up on correcting players who couldn't tell the difference <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T19:06:46-08:00","id":1424409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zahana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424408#post1424408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have 14 Clans because people keep referring to the Salubri as a Clan instead of a Bloodline. The line got too blurred and they just gave up on correcting players who couldn't tell the difference <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, it's accurate because Saulot is back as an Antediluvian and Tremere is temporarily one due to the sacrifice of the Antitribu.<br /> <br /> Ravnos is gone so I guess the Ravnos are a Bloodline?<br /> <br /> Are Hecata a Bloodline or a Clan since Augustus is probably dead-dead but not necessarily diablerized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T19:22:10-08:00","id":1424412,"title":"","content":"Is he though? Cause from my understanding Mr. Big White Worm was housed somewhere in Vienna and with the Vienna Chantry falling down and going boom there's no telling if it survived.<br /> <br /> Until the Player's Companion comes out I'm not considering Ravnos anything more than Caitiff.<br /> <br /> Is Uncle Augie really dead? We don't know that. Who's to say the Capuchin didn't drag his body into Oblivion and bind him there using some lost ceremony found in the libraries of the Shadow Temple. Or possibly someone gave the esteem Giovanni progenitor the big slurp allowing the different bloodlines to become united under the Hecata banner and the merging of souls is why they have Cappadocian disciplines but the Giovanni bite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T19:48:35-08:00","id":1424422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424407#post1424407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The reason can be &quot;We decided we want more clans.&quot; It's fiction, it's made up. It's not a real thing, nor does it describe a real thing. Of course any such decision would be contextualized, but it looks like they're going to call the Salubri a clan anyway, so we're already past the triskadeka event horizon.<br /> <br /> The succession of the Tremere over the Salubri isn't because there were 13 clans, it's because the Tremere wanted the power of having a third generation founder.<br /> <br /> It doesn't erode the lore. There are a lot of things in V5 that I personally feel erodes the <i>game</i> but I do not believe any of it particularly erodes the lore. One of the things about a fictional setting is that we're always going be learning new things about the setting, we're going to learn things that recontextualize what we already know, and we're going to learn things that may contradict what we knew before. This has been the case for sure since first edition, and since 13 is just a number, it's fine if there are 14 or 15 or 16 or 12. The Book of Nod itself, like all accounts of Cainite history, isn't bound to be historically factual within the game itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like any work of fiction, symbolism in text makes a difference, and that is what you get with the number 13. Fact is, it is the reason why the creators deliberately went up to 13 Clans in the first place. It\u2019s not like *I* chose the number of Clans being 13 and made it canon - it was the creators. Whatever they saw as important as a symbol in the game hasn\u2019t really changed with V5 - which also explicitly refers to 13 Clans. Personally, I just think it loses symbolism and a particular atmosphere - that the writers themselves established - to hand wave the symbolism away in a cavalier fashion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The difference between a bloodline and a clan is like the difference between a planet and a dwarf planet. It may not be arbitrary, but it's a semantic distinction based on features deemed to make something a planet or a dwarf planet, and such definitions could change in the future.<br /> <br /> First edition Vampire said there might only be nine antediluvians or as many as 27, so the idea that &quot;there were always 13 antediluvians&quot; isn't even accurate. </div> </div> </div>Well, it's a change of subject, but the precise reason why Pluto was finally declassified from a \u2018Planet' to a 'Dwarf Planet' was that it couldn\u2019t guarantee a clear orbit around the Sun. It wasn\u2019t just a semantic distinction, but in any case, it\u2019s not really a precise analogy to compare with 13 Clans. Fact is, \u201913\u2019 will remain a mystical number for all sorts of cultural reasons whether or not Vampire chooses to have 13 Clans. If Vampire ceases to have 13 Clans it will just mean the game is no longer able to tap into whatever symbolism is associated with the number 13 - which I think is a shame for aesthetic reasons.<br /> <br /> What first edition did, regarding Antediluvians, was allude to writings in the \u2018biblical\u2019 text of the Book of Nod that mentioned '13 Tribes', and then created a <i>mystery</i> that implied there could be 13 Antediluvians <i>or possibly more, </i>as children of Caine. That mystery fueled much of the backstory and meta plot of the game over the years. By just making 14 Clans, and essentially making it clear that 13 is no longer a significant number (and by extension, making the writings in the Book of Nod redundant) it reduces the mystery in the game. Thereby affecting the atmosphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 11-16-2020, 10:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T21:04:55-08:00","id":1424450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424422#post1424422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like any work of fiction, symbolism in text makes a difference, and that is what you get with the number 13. Fact is, it is the reason why the creators deliberately went up to 13 Clans in the first place. It\u2019s not like *I* chose the number of Clans being 13 and made it canon - it was the creators. Whatever they saw as important as a symbol in the game hasn\u2019t really changed with V5 - which also explicitly refers to 13 Clans. Personally, I just think it loses symbolism and a particular atmosphere - that the writers themselves established - to hand wave the symbolism away in a cavalier fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing about an IP that's existed for decades and has had dozens of people work on it is that it can be and often does turn out to be mutable. I also think it's pretty insulting to suggest that the current people working on the IP naming more than 13 clans are just cavalierly handwaving it away. And naming the Salubri a clan is <i>fine</i> because they were a clan, and the only reason they were no longer called a clan is because of the destruction of their founder, Saulot, who as it appears, was still active.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424422#post1424422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it's a change of subject, but the precise reason why Pluto was finally declassified from a \u2018Planet' to a 'Dwarf Planet' was that it couldn\u2019t guarantee a clear orbit around the Sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you understand that my point was that this was based on a definition of &quot;planet&quot; that was invented by humans, and that the people involved could have instead chosen to alter the definition of planet to include Pluto? The definition would likely also include many other objects as planets, and that's probably suboptimal, but it is something we could do and something that has been seriously proposed.<br /> <br /> All of these categories are descriptions of things, whether real or fictional, and these definitions can change over time if needed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424422#post1424422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wasn\u2019t just a semantic distinction, but in any case, it\u2019s not really a precise analogy to compare with 13 Clans. Fact is, \u201913\u2019 will remain a mystical number for all sorts of cultural reasons whether or not Vampire chooses to have 13 Clans. If Vampire ceases to have 13 Clans it will just mean the game is no longer able to tap into whatever symbolism is associated with the number 13 - which I think is a shame for aesthetic reasons.<br /> <br /> What first edition did, regarding Antediluvians, was allude to writings in the \u2018biblical\u2019 text of the Book of Nod that mentioned '13 Tribes', and then created a <i>mystery</i> that implied there could be 13 Antediluvians <i>or possibly more, </i>as children of Caine. That mystery fueled much of the backstory and meta plot of the game over the years. By just making 14 Clans, and essentially making it clear that 13 is no longer a significant number (and by extension, making the writings in the Book of Nod redundant) it reduces the mystery in the game. Thereby affecting the atmosphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it were a precise analogy to the 13 clans, it'd just be the 13 clans. Analogies are by nature imprecise. In this case the analogy is: &quot;Clan&quot; is a category in a work of fiction to define one way a group of vampires connected by lineage can exist. Another is &quot;bloodline,&quot; and vampires with seemingly no blood connections are &quot;Caitiff.&quot; Categories are by their nature constructed as ways to explain things. And over time those categories can change and be used differently. For example defining Ventrue as a clan even though they claimed they'd destroyed their antediluvian founder (highly suspect claim) but then defining the Harbingers of Skulls as a bloodline, despite them being members of the Cappadocian clan, and defining the Salubri as a bloodline because there are so few of them, or continuing to define the Ravnos as a clan just because despite the Week of Nightmares. It's clearly an arbitrary system, and the Salubri are themselves as deserving of being called a clan as any other as their founder was literally one of the thirteen antediluvians in the Book of Nod you keep citing.<br /> <br /> Vampire 1e also claimed there were seven antediluvians, but only two had names known to modern kindred - Lucian and Mekhet (although Arikel is also named so). Obviously that changed over time and was clearly not set in stone (and who Lucian and Mekhet are has never been nailed down). Vlad's letter to Mina numbers them at possibly 9, 27, 100, and 0, but that text is just as in-character and reliable as the Book of Nod.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it's just a number, and we get Banu Haqim, Brujah, Gangrel, Lasombra, Malkavian, The Ministry, Nosferatu, Ravnos, Salubri, Toreador, Tremere, Tzimisce, Ventrue, and whatever they go with regarding the Giovanni, whether it's the Hecata as in the as-yet unpublished Cults of the Blood Gods, or something else. And it'll be fine. Nothing of value will be lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T21:26:14-08:00","id":1424457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zahana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424408#post1424408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have 14 Clans because people keep referring to the Salubri as a Clan instead of a Bloodline. The line got too blurred and they just gave up on correcting players who couldn't tell the difference <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is my favorite explanation, and I regret not seeing it sooner.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T21:52:47-08:00","id":1424460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424450#post1424450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing about an IP that's existed for decades and has had dozens of people work on it is that it can be and often does turn out to be mutable. I also think it's pretty insulting to suggest that the current people working on the IP naming more than 13 clans are just cavalierly handwaving it away. And naming the Salubri a clan is <i>fine</i> because they were a clan, and the only reason they were no longer called a clan is because of the destruction of their founder, Saulot, who as it appears, was still active.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m saying that the people on this forum who are just dismissing 13 Clans as \u2018just a number\u2019 are being cavalier. I\u2019ve yet to see what the justification of Justin Achilli, et al is, but I do think it is a point worth addressing. In the actual promotion video, people are asked for feedback on the upcoming content of the Companion. That is mine, in part at least - I want to know what the justification is for abandoning the canon regarding 13 Clans?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you understand that my point was that this was based on a definition of &quot;planet&quot; that was invented by humans, and that the people involved could have instead chosen to alter the definition of planet to include Pluto? The definition would likely also include many other objects as planets, and that's probably suboptimal, but it is something we could do and something that has been seriously proposed. </div> </div> </div>I just see it as a bad analogy (and a quick disclosure that I actually teach this stuff professionally). The issue of whether or not Pluto is a planet or not is based on factual evidence - it was disqualified for the purposes of scientific clarity. In the case of 13 Clans for Vampire, it is, as you pointed out, a work of fiction that draws inspiration from supernatural folklore and symbolism - including the number 13. It is not as if you redefine the meanings held in the symbolism of the game based on facts and evidence - it\u2019s purely aesthetic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All of these categories are descriptions of things, whether real or fictional, and these definitions can change over time if needed. </div> </div> </div>No they don\u2019t - the processes by which things are defined in both respects are entirely unrelated. It is a bad analogy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampire 1e also claimed there were seven antediluvians, but only two had names known to modern kindred - Lucian and Mekhet (although Arikel is also named so). Obviously that changed over time and was clearly not set in stone (and who Lucian and Mekhet are has never been nailed down). Vlad's letter to Mina numbers them at possibly 9, 27, 100, and 0, but that text is just as in-character and reliable as the Book of Nod. </div> </div> </div>V1 claimed seven Antediluvians existed <i>still, </i>although this remained a mystery. Regardless, the 13 Tribes mentioned in the Book of Nod is the key reference to Clans, while the number 13 is referenced in a number of other ways too. It\u2019s written as a significant 'in game' number, that is given reverence by the characters within vampire society as much as anything else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway, it's just a number, and we get Banu Haqim, Brujah, Gangrel, Lasombra, Malkavian, The Ministry, Nosferatu, Ravnos, Salubri, Toreador, Tremere, Tzimisce, Ventrue, and whatever they go with regarding the Giovanni, whether it's the Hecata as in the as-yet unpublished Cults of the Blood Gods, or something else. And it'll be fine. Nothing of value will be lost. </div> </div> </div>Well, its a subjective view, but I just think it is entirely crap to lose that particular symbol and the game is less atmospheric for it. So, no, I don\u2019t think it is fine and something of value has been lost to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 11-17-2020, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T22:24:16-08:00","id":1424463,"title":"","content":"<br /> <i><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zahana</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have 14 Clans because people keep referring to the Salubri as a Clan instead of a Bloodline. The line got too blurred and they just gave up on correcting players who couldn't tell the difference <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div></i><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is my favorite explanation, and I regret not seeing it sooner.</div> </div> </div> </div>And now people will get confused all over again!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 11-17-2020, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T23:29:48-08:00","id":1424470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424460#post1424460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m saying that the people on this forum who are just dismissing 13 Clans as \u2018just a number\u2019 are being cavalier. I\u2019ve yet to see what the justification of Justin Achilli, et al is, but I do think it is a point worth addressing. In the actual promotion video, people are asked for feedback on the upcoming content of the Companion. That is mine, in part at least - I want to know what the justification is for abandoning the canon regarding 13 Clans?</div> </div> </div> </div>No new clans have been added, though? The Salubri were here all along, and in the setting, longer than the Tremere. The decision to call any clan a bloodline or not is already demonstrably arbitrary in the cases of the Ventrue, Tzimisce, Lasombra, Tremere, Giovanni, Brujah, Salubri, Cappadocians, and Ravnos.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424460#post1424460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just see it as a bad analogy (and a quick disclosure that I actually teach this stuff professionally). The issue of whether or not Pluto is a planet or not is based on factual evidence - it was disqualified for the purposes of scientific clarity. In the case of 13 Clans for Vampire, it is, as you pointed out, a work of fiction that draws inspiration from supernatural folklore and symbolism - including the number 13. It is not as if you redefine the meanings held in the symbolism of the game based on facts and evidence - it\u2019s purely aesthetic.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point was that how we interpret those facts and evidence is based on something humans decided. There is no such thing as a category of &quot;planet&quot; or &quot;dwarf planet&quot; in the universe, except for humans creating those categories to place existing objects into, but categories are abstractions necessary to describe and explain the universe - this doesn't grant them objective meaning, and over time the meanings they do have may change. Pluto's a dwarf planet because of how humans decided to define &quot;planet&quot; in the first place. Yes, that definition is based on empirical observations, but again, you can find stuff like this:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://ilovetheuniverse.com/scientists-want-to-change-the-definition-of-planet\" target=\"_blank\">https://ilovetheuniverse.com/scienti...tion-of-planet</a><br /> <br /> because the definition is what we say it is. If we want planets to fit a different criteria, then Pluto is a planet again. But then so would a lot of other objects, like our Moon. Is that desirable? I don't know, but it's not beyond the realm of possibility.<br /> <br /> Similarly, when looking at how bloodlines and clans are defined in Vampire, one can still go back and just say &quot;Salubri are a clan despite being hunted to near extinction because they were always a clan.&quot; That is, in-character, in-game, some Kindred might just shrug and say &quot;They're a clan as far as I'm concerned&quot; and that's valid. It doesn't violate anything. Or Cainite scholars could just acknowledge the distinction is arbitrary and it's not as if the Tremere are super powerful enough to make a big fuss about it.<br /> <br /> The analogy is that in each case you have two categories with certain criteria to fit into one, with those that don't fit going into the second. But also, the definition of either could change for any number of reasons. That's the connection.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424460#post1424460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V1 claimed seven Antediluvians existed <i>still, </i>although this remained a mystery. Regardless, the 13 Tribes mentioned in the Book of Nod is the key reference to Clans, while the number 13 is referenced in a number of other ways too. It\u2019s written as a significant 'in game' number, that is given reverence by the characters within vampire society as much as anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the word &quot;still&quot; was definitely not in there, and it wasn't sufficiently contextualized to imply it, IMO.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424460#post1424460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, its a subjective view, but I just think it is entirely crap to lose that particular symbol and the game is less atmospheric for it. So, no, I don\u2019t think it is fine and something of value has been lost to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's fine - your feelings are valid. I get it. I just don't think it's going to harm the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 11-17-2020, 02:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T23:31:48-08:00","id":1424471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424463#post1424463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And now people will get confused all over again!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh hell.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I like the explanation better, even though it's purely OOC.<br /> <br /> That said I do also like the idea of Cainite scholars disagreeing over who does and does not qualify as a clan, and whether any such arguing would result in a shift in perceptions anywhere else in Cainite society. I feel like the shift from Salubri to Tremere and Cappadocian to Giovanni wouldn't exactly be universally supported, and it's only commonly accepted in modern times because of inertia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T23:51:59-08:00","id":1424473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424470#post1424470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No new clans have been added, though? The Salubri were here all along, and in the setting, longer than the Tremere. The decision to call any clan a bloodline or not is already demonstrably arbitrary in the cases of the Ventrue, Tzimisce, Lasombra, Tremere, Giovanni, Brujah, Salubri, Cappadocians, and Ravnos.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were originally a Clan, but as per canon, were only a Bloodline by modern nights, and very rare to the extent that they were practically mythical.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The point was that how we interpret those facts and evidence is based on something humans decided. There is no such thing as a category of &quot;planet&quot; or &quot;dwarf planet&quot; in the universe, except for humans creating those categories to place existing objects into, but categories are abstractions necessary to describe and explain the universe - this doesn't grant them objective meaning, and over time the meanings they do have may change. Pluto's a dwarf planet because of how humans decided to define &quot;planet&quot; in the first place. Yes, that definition is based on empirical observations, but again, you can find stuff like this:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://ilovetheuniverse.com/scientists-want-to-change-the-definition-of-planet\" target=\"_blank\">https://ilovetheuniverse.com/scienti...tion-of-planet</a><br /> <br /> because the definition is what we say it is. If we want planets to fit a different criteria, then Pluto is a planet again. But then so would a lot of other objects, like our Moon. Is that desirable? I don't know, but it's not beyond the realm of possibility. </div> </div> </div>Again it is a sidetrack, but actually no. The definition criteria that essentially demoted Pluto from being a planet is that it couldn\u2019t guarantee it could orbit a clear path around the Sun. This was because of it\u2019s eccentric orbital motion, which suggests it will collide with another body (Neptune) in due course. The definition of \u2018planet\u2019 itself wasn\u2019t the issue, although there had been lots of debate over the size of Pluto and the fact that as a relatively recent discovery itself there had been other discoveries since of orbiting bodies that were larger/nearer than Pluto. However, the deciding factor was that it couldn\u2019t fulfill the existing definition of a planet because it couldn\u2019t guarantee its orbit - it was the most objective point that was raised in the debate at the time. The more recent term of Dwarf Planet was adopted instead.<br /> <br /> Either way, it really doesn\u2019t have much to do with the canon of Vampire, as it is based on scientific evidence and factual clarity, rather than simply to do with narrative aesthetics, so it is still not a great analogy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, the word &quot;still&quot; was definitely not in there, and it wasn't sufficiently contextualized to imply it, IMO. </div> </div> </div>I think it was, by the virtue of the discussion of 13 Tribes mentioned in the Book of Nod.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, that's fine - your feelings are valid. I get it. I just don't think it's going to harm the game. </div> </div> </div>Fine from this end too. We can agree to disagree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 11-17-2020, 03:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-17T00:44:26-08:00","id":1424477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424473#post1424473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fine from this end too. We can agree to disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair!<br /> <br /> Except that my analogy's good.<br /> <br /> Also, read the link - it's cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-17T01:30:34-08:00","id":1424485,"title":"","content":"I think the average vampire won't care about the Bloodline/Clan distinction. Scholars will, and snobs will, but the average lick on the ground probably doesn't care if you call the Salubri a Clan or a Bloodline, and technically both answers are true, depending on your perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-17T21:28:51-08:00","id":1424651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424409#post1424409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically, it's accurate because Saulot is back as an Antediluvian and Tremere is temporarily one due to the sacrifice of the Antitribu.<br /> <br /> Ravnos is gone so I guess the Ravnos are a Bloodline?<br /> <br /> Are Hecata a Bloodline or a Clan since Augustus is probably dead-dead but not necessarily diablerized.</div> </div> </div> </div>The death of the Founder doesn't mean that Clan ceases to be a Clan. In <i>Gehenna</i> they revealed that several of the original Antediluvians were long dead, including [Ventrue]. The death of [Ravnos] doesn't mean that his Clan is no longer a Clan. The near extinction of the Ravnos in the Week of Nightmares could have put them into Bloodline status but that doesn't necessarily mean they are in V5. Also that was twenty years ago. Hell, while the V5 Rulebook does say they were near extinct, it also lumped them in with the Giovanni and as we now know, that's factually wrong.<br /> <br /> The Hecata are a Clan though one that almost borders on being a Sect. Yes, Augustus is dead but it's heavily implied he was killed in a ritual to unify the various Bloodlines of Death with the Giovanni to create a create a Clan or remake the Clan. Hence why everyone suddenly has the Giovanni Flaw or why the Harbingers can suddenly Embrace again.<br /> <br /> As for the Salubri and their Clan/Bloodline status, it really depends on what's going to happen to them in V5. If the Castes reunite, I could see them reestablishing themselves as a Clan. How that will happen and what they will as a whole, I cannot say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-18T10:59:24-08:00","id":1424781,"title":"","content":"I also wondered if the marketing material is just a generalisation. Maybe they're calling the Salubri a Clan for noobs, as that's an accessible idea for people who aren't hung up on the lore, but they might call them a Bloodline in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 11-20-2020, 03:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-18T11:50:18-08:00","id":1424793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424781#post1424781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also wondered if the marketing material is just a generalisation. Maybe they're calling the Salubri a Clan for noobs, as that's an accessible idea for people who aren't hung up on the lore, but they might call them a Bloodline on the book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Bloodline and clan are relatively intuitive terms for native speakers. <br /> Also I think Salubri are one of the less friendly bloodlines for newer players. Newer players should gravitate towards the Brujah, Toreador, Malkavians, Nosferatu, Gangrel, Caitiff, perhaps the Ventrue. Though that might be me thinking of prior editions too much since physical Disciplines are now just as complicated as socials or mentals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-18T17:20:21-08:00","id":1424831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424781#post1424781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also wondered if the marketing material is just a generalisation. Maybe they're calling the Salubri a Clan for noobs, as that's an accessible idea for people who aren't hung up on the lore, but they might call them a Bloodline on the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, the Salubri are extremely lore heavy. Even if the player doesn't need to know it, it's highly relevant in a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T06:26:20-08:00","id":1424923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424115#post1424115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but we already have revised,revised didn't cease to exist. Don't you want something new?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not pointed at me, but I think many will agree.<br /> <br /> In short: NO. I want more stuff along the lines I liked about this game, not a rewrite. &quot;Updated&quot; does not equal to &quot;new&quot;. You can update the setting, add new rules tools and concepts, make the system run more smoothly, whatever. What you shouldn't do is changing everything to a point that it feels more like a rewrite than an update. For many, including me, V5 went too far.<br /> <br /> If you want a &quot;new&quot; game, then write a new game. Worked for Requiem 2e, much better than the half-assed 1e. Don't make screw up what many people liked and slap an old logo on it, because of brand recognition. Didn't work for D&amp;D 4e, didn't work for NWoD, didn't wotrk for many games and it splitted he WoD fandom greatly this time again. Someone should learn the lesson.<br /> <br /> Sorry if it was unconventionally harsh for me, I'm a bit sleep deprived (damn cat...) and it's something that bugs me for years.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T07:01:23-08:00","id":1424927,"title":"","content":"For various reasons (part of it being my distaste both for V5 and the community reaction, pro and con, to it), I dropped off as far as V5 news goes.<br /> <br /> Can someone please give me a TLDR rundown of what has been happening? I recall Sir Edgelord von Fangstein being dropped as creative lead or something, and a slapdown from Paradox, but why is there now a third (fourth, fifth?) company releasing (and writing?) the books?<br /> <br /> In short: WAT?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T07:13:36-08:00","id":1424928,"title":"","content":"In short... Modiphius has lost the license for WoD IPs, that is now in the hands of a different company. Officially all the involved parties are being tight lipped about the reasons why. Unofficially, it is probably related to the slow rate of production on the part of Modiphius and the debatable quality of what they did produce. For now the changes will, in theory, not impact the work of Onyx Path does with the IP and will probably see more books released in the future from Renegades Studio.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T07:41:26-08:00","id":1424931,"title":"","content":"Is V5 good yet, or can I go back to hugging my V20 tome?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T07:42:49-08:00","id":1424932,"title":"","content":"Nothing's been changed. So if you didn't like it on release, you won't like it now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T07:44:43-08:00","id":1424934,"title":"","content":"Thanks. Back to the shadows I go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T08:45:45-08:00","id":1424942,"title":"","content":"I have to disagree, this entire push seems like Paradox is caving to the fans who didn't like V5's limited options and scope in the initial release.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gogo Baccala<br /> <br /> Drag Queen, Ex-Attorney, Freelance Deity","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26376-gogobaccala","name":"Gogobaccala","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T08:46:36-08:00","id":1424944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424934#post1424934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. Back to the shadows I go.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Their is a 'yet' on nothings been changed, so we shall see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T08:58:00-08:00","id":1424947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gogobaccala</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424942#post1424942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to disagree, this entire push seems like Paradox is caving to the fans who didn't like V5's limited options and scope in the initial release.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be that Paradox is the one who's forcing the V5ism's, and demanding more sales, whilst Mophidius might be people who wanted to backpedal from V5isms. Or it could be Paradox screaming in despair at a bunch of developers who've been drinking same the koolaid. Unless you know someone on the inside, it's speculation, and we can only use what's been released to us: V5 remains just as V5 as it did on release.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T10:18:09-08:00","id":1424967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424923#post1424923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not pointed at me, but I think many will agree.<br /> <br /> In short: NO. I want more stuff along the lines I liked about this game, not a rewrite. &amp;quot;Updated&amp;quot; does not equal to &amp;quot;new&amp;quot;. You can update the setting, add new rules tools and concepts, make the system run more smoothly, whatever. What you shouldn't do is changing everything to a point that it feels more like a rewrite than an update. For many, including me, V5 went too far.<br /> <br /> If you want a &amp;quot;new&amp;quot; game, then write a new game. Worked for Requiem 2e, much better than the half-assed 1e. Don't make screw up what many people liked and slap an old logo on it, because of brand recognition. Didn't work for D&amp;D 4e, didn't work for NWoD, didn't wotrk for many games and it splitted he WoD fandom greatly this time again. Someone should learn the lesson.<br /> <br /> Sorry if it was unconventionally harsh for me, I'm a bit sleep deprived (damn cat...) and it's something that bugs me for years.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T12:35:27-08:00","id":1424991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gogobaccala</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424942#post1424942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to disagree, this entire push seems like Paradox is caving to the fans who didn't like V5's limited options and scope in the initial release.</div> </div> </div> </div>Caving is a really negative way to put it. It does seem that they're moving away from some early decisions, but I wouldn't expect a full blown paradigm shift from V5.<br /> <br /> For me, the change gives me hope V5 will be something I like vs. the direction Martin signaled previously wasn't something I wanted to have anything to do with. And with a different possible direction (we'll see with the Companion and Sabbat books) V5 itself is more appealing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T12:41:37-08:00","id":1424994,"title":"","content":"Caving isn't negative. It's the culmination of three years of various forces finally pressuring corporate into making products people want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gogo Baccala<br /> <br /> Drag Queen, Ex-Attorney, Freelance Deity","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26376-gogobaccala","name":"Gogobaccala","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T14:34:56-08:00","id":1425014,"title":"","content":"Lol they won't change anything and you will still buy it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T15:52:00-08:00","id":1425031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425014#post1425014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lol they won't change anything and you will still buy it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I only finally gave V5 a substantive look this month, some two years and three months after publication, after I learned Achilli was working on the line. If the line continues according to the sort of material Martin said we should expect, I'll just go back to the 20th anniversary edition books, or perhaps to some other IP entirely. If Paradox's continued treatment of the line is vastly improved from the trainwreck that was the Camarilla book and edits to Changing Ways, then I'll stick with it. Given that this sort of thing is precisely why Paradox cleaned house, I don't expect that to be the case.<br /> <br /> We're not all slaves to brands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 11-19-2020, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T16:09:54-08:00","id":1425035,"title":"","content":"But there's a lot of windbag complaints with V5. I might say I don't like it because reasons a,b,c... maybe even get to yyy,yyz,yza,yzb.... <br /> <br /> But then I also see apparently professional reviewers thinking the game is too adult for them with the biting... or the game is secretly hitler.... y'know, generally fucking silly stuff. Some of the possitive reviews are the most.... misleading. How do we know people are making sense of things? corperate producer types are notoriously dense at times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T16:19:24-08:00","id":1425040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425014#post1425014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lol they won't change anything and you will still buy it.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Threadcrapping never helped anyone, Dwight.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T16:21:37-08:00","id":1425042,"title":"","content":"In any case, as long as they keep a gritty horror-movie high generation Neonate focus and the Anarchs vs. Camarilla, I'll be fine. I'm glad the Sabbat is coming back as they're a big source of drama but I also felt they lost a lot of their bite due to becoming too &quot;known.&quot; It was basically like Apocalypse. If Apocalypse shows up once in a blue moon to fight the X-men, he's a terrifying and awesome bad guy.<br /> <br /> If he shows up constantly, he's a joke.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat need to be handled with care and I hope the book they publish about them goes beyond Black Dog to be utterly terrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T16:22:14-08:00","id":1425043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425035#post1425035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there's a lot of windbag complaints with V5. I might say I don't like it because reasons a,b,c... maybe even get to yyy,yyz,yza,yzb....<br /> <br /> But then I also see apparently professional reviewers thinking the game is too adult for them with the biting... or the game is secretly hitler.... y'know, generally fucking silly stuff. Some of the possitive reviews are the most.... misleading. How do we know people are making sense of things? corperate producer types are notoriously dense at times.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't really looked at professional reviews. New WW's approach turned me off early on, later events solidified that impression, and now I'm going with my own perceptions while actually reading the book.<br /> <br /> My initial reaction is that I disagree with a lot of the complaints I've seen just on this forum, but I am hesitant to give my own disagreement much credence without trying these things in play.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T16:27:04-08:00","id":1425047,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest, I liked V5 but I didn't feel it came into its own until Chicago by Night V5.<br /> <br /> I feel like it had a lot of good ideas but OPP was necessary to sandpaper the edges.<br /> <br /> I also feel like Jason Carl made a substantial contribution by making LA by Night illustrate how it's &quot;supposed&quot; to be played.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T16:47:02-08:00","id":1425056,"title":"","content":"I'll see how the Companion shakes out and if I like it I'll go for the rest of the line.<br /> <br /> I have trouble sitting through streamed RPG sessions for some reason, might be the ADHD. I want to, though. I want to see how that chronicle went.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T00:15:21-08:00","id":1425099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424831#post1424831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know, the Salubri are extremely lore heavy. Even if the player doesn't need to know it, it's highly relevant in a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>But my point is that it's just a line in a press release (and some related chatter online). We shouldn't extrapolate that to mean that the Salubri have been elevated to clan status just yet. <br /> <br /> Press releases are for journalists as much as players. A journo who doesn't know VTM won't care that the Salubri are really a bloodline. And it's easier to say '3 new clans' than '2 new clans and 1 bloodline'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T02:56:03-08:00","id":1425114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1424191#post1424191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s a number that every previous edition of the game made a big deal of. It is why they have always quite explicitly referred to \u201c13 Clans\u201d in every edition of the game - including the first edition, even though we didn\u2019t know who the other six were. It is also why they developed the term \u201cBloodline\u201d to refer to lineages of vampire outside of the 13 Clans, and why the Tremere\u2019s ascent significantly was diablerie at the expense of the Salubri. It was a number that added to the atmosphere of the game, giving it a biblical/occult feel as much as trying to link the lore of the game to Cain and the 13 Antediluvians.<br /> <br /> Now people are saying, &quot;it\u2019s just a number\u201d. Great. To me, it\u2019s just a meta plot development to ignore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Recently, either Achilli or some other big gun of WoD said on twitter that they always loved the idea that there was a common misintepretation in Noddist lore about the numbers. There were not 13 clans but 3 by 10, meaning there could be over 30+ Antediluvians across the world, forgotten and re-emerging bloodlines, anomalies like the Drowned ec etc. Looks like the creators of the game think differently.<br /> As for me, I love this approach. More mysteries and additions to the canon without removing the previous lines are always welcome.<br /> <br /> Lore purism should go away.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T03:08:05-08:00","id":1425119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425114#post1425114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lore purism should go away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ancient mysteries should remain ancient mysteries.<br /> <br /> But making big sweeping retcons to contemporary material? Eh. No. Especially when the new stuff doesn't seem to fully understand what it replaced, and generally seems worse than whatever it was people fell in love with, even without the bias of familiarity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T03:27:15-08:00","id":1425122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425047#post1425047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be honest, I liked V5 but I didn't feel it came into its own until Chicago by Night V5.<br /> <br /> [\u2026]<br /> <br /> I also feel like Jason Carl made a substantial contribution by making LA by Night illustrate how it's &quot;supposed&quot; to be played.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel the same way, but about Cults of the Blood Gods instead of Chicago by Night. CotBG was the first publication, where I had the feeling that there was a clear plan behind what V5 wants to do lore wise and in which ways it wants to differ from V20. (But to be honest: I read CotBG before I read CbN.)<br /> <br /> I agree on LA by Night. Jason Carl's narration and world building is pretty evocative and inspiring. But for me it was the mixture of LA by Night and Vein Pursuit. I like Jason for his atmospheric world building, but seeing Kareem's chronicle was really great for getting to know the new system with it's differences. Seeing Jason handle the rules was confusing, because I often thought that I was the one misinterpreting something.<br /> <br /> So yes, d'accord with everything you said, but extra love for Kareem from me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">&quot;Life's barely long enough to get good at one thing. So be careful what you get good at.&quot;</span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26196-saturno","name":"Saturno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T03:44:34-08:00","id":1425126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1423325#post1423325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are trying to convince who of what here?<br /> If we exclude DAV20, the racist aspects of the setting sharply declined with revised. There are issues, but it's not with the Ravnos. However, whitewashing seems to be a growing problem, and the setting seems to be getting a lot more 'noblebright'. In my opinion, it's lost all comedic edge and seems to be catering more towards a narrow subsection of society at the expense of others.</div> </div> </div> </div>yes, V5 introduced the woke police feature to supervise all the Vampire games and put those who attempt to play edgy characters like Tzimisce Nazi or racist Romani stereotypes into SJW reeducation camps.<br /> Seriously, this never gets old. You do you. If you don't like the theme and mood of V5 play V20, or Dark Ages or write your own V6.<br /> In regards to the last part, which repeats the rightwing or 'centrist' youtubers gospel, consider the next:<br /> 1) the 'subsection' is not so narrow neither simply a subsection. Picturing it as such means you are trying to downgrade the subject and the problems many vulnerable groups and their allies are vocal about to disparage and present those as insignificant.<br /> 2) none of the other groups are suffering because the core book removed lots of not-so-comedic edgy stuff<br /> 3) edge can be written and played without overstepping it. The right combination of tactfulness and daring in exploring controversial topics is a real challenge so I don't mind WW, Paradox etc playing a safe card. This is primary reason they shifted the tone in V5, not because of imaginary wokefulness attacking the mindsets of the Western gamers or whatever is preached by V5 hate squad.<br /> <br /> I have my concerns with V5 corebook, but not with the supposed 'noblebright' as if this word could ever define anything in WoD. I did not like the style, the layout and the writing which sounded even juvenile at times. But not the direction to actually listen to previously mischaracterised, stereotyped and misunderstood groups and properly mirroring the changes in common attitude towards these groups irl in the WoD.<br /> By the way, they are going to invite diversity readers for the next books, probably for all of them. I hope that won't hurt anyone's feelings? <br /> <br /> I can only imagine what dumpster fire will explode in these forums when they finall do Sabbat V5 (which I am eagerly looking forward as I played 95% Sabbat for the last 10+ years) and it &quot;surprisingly&quot; does not contain stuff like Chechnya chapter.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T04:10:34-08:00","id":1425133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425119#post1425119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ancient mysteries should remain ancient mysteries.<br /> <br /> But making big sweeping retcons to contemporary material? Eh. No. Especially when the new stuff doesn't seem to fully understand what it replaced, and generally seems worse than whatever it was people fell in love with, even without the bias of familiarity.</div> </div> </div> </div>It most probably will happen anyway, as the creators of the game including the Revised master Achilli, are expressing interest towards such developments. I fell in love with the old stuff too and am glad it receives a major shakeup (it grew too set in stone).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T04:57:12-08:00","id":1425139,"title":"","content":"A shakeup's fine. I just wish these things were less contrivances upon contrivances. <br /> <br /> The Giovanni finally having a Coup... That's organic. That had proper build up. That's a nice thing to spice up the setting. <br /> <br /> The Gehanna war, the complete reshuffling of The Anarchs, Cam and Sabbat, the Second inquisition... That's like... stretches upon stretches to the point of Farce. <br /> <br /> and the complete rework of disciplines and how vampires work... It's one thing to change mechanics, it's another thing to have them completely upend the story. <br /> <br /> More Ur-Shulgi waking up, more the giovanni finally boiling over. Less &quot;What if we made thin blood more desirable than thick blood&quot; or &quot;Let's make Setite factions out of the viewpoints of the most extreme 5%&quot; or &quot;let's just end thaumaturgy paths, ok?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T07:30:28-08:00","id":1425158,"title":"","content":"I see you mentioning a lot that you\u2019re upset at them removing the Paths from Blood Sorcery, but what\u2019s stopping you from simply adding them back in? The Blood Rituals section of the core book encourages Storytellers and Players to come up with rituals that fit their characters and Chronicles, so why not do that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25976-differentjustin","name":"DifferentJustin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T09:02:26-08:00","id":1425173,"title":"","content":"Mechanically, because in an edition where virtually everything's weaker, it's not really reasonable to restore something to strength. Puting paths back in would do be doing that. And making everything strong again... might as well just play a better edition where I don't need to do so much work to make things work. Also because I need to spend far more XP just to make a rounded out fledgling in this edition; I don't have the luxury of buying paths and rituals when I need attributes and abilities if I want my character to make the year long mark. <br /> Storywise, because getting rid of paths is wrong, and making them rituals doesn't fix that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T10:51:33-08:00","id":1425189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425114#post1425114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Recently, either Achilli or some other big gun of WoD said on twitter that they always loved the idea that there was a common misintepretation in Noddist lore about the numbers. There were not 13 clans but 3 by 10, meaning there could be over 30+ Antediluvians across the world, forgotten and re-emerging bloodlines, anomalies like the Drowned ec etc. Looks like the creators of the game think differently.<br /> As for me, I love this approach. More mysteries and additions to the canon without removing the previous lines are always welcome.<br /> <br /> Lore purism should go away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conversely, I hate the approach. Not least because if they just add Clan upon Clan upon Clan, then we will inevitably just end up with a load of badly designed ones and the game itself will lose any sense of background focus it had for what would be, in effect, the inclusion of a bunch of Prestige Classes. Less mystery, less symbolism and just a bunch of power fantasy to replace it with. I don\u2019t buy the crap about \u2018misinterpretation' of the Book of Nod either - it actually lists the 13 Clans by name.<br /> <br /> If whoever mentioned that the Clan/Bloodline confusion could just be unspecific marketing talk, then maybe that is it. If so, some of the other justifications here will look silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T12:04:42-08:00","id":1425209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425189#post1425189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Conversely, I hate the approach. Not least because if they just add Clan upon Clan upon Clan, then we will inevitably just end up with a load of badly designed ones and the game itself will lose any sense of background focus it had for what would be, in effect, the inclusion of a bunch of Prestige Classes. Less mystery, less symbolism and just a bunch of power fantasy to replace it with. I don\u2019t buy the crap about \u2018misinterpretation' of the Book of Nod either - it actually lists the 13 Clans by name.<br /> <br /> If whoever mentioned that the Clan/Bloodline confusion could just be unspecific marketing talk, then maybe that is it. If so, some of the other justifications here will look silly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So the number &quot;13&quot; is not a silly symbolism already? What else, was the Third Generation embraced on the Halloween night, or Friday 13?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T14:17:13-08:00","id":1425237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425189#post1425189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Conversely, I hate the approach. Not least because if they just add Clan upon Clan upon Clan, then we will inevitably just end up with a load of badly designed ones and the game itself will lose any sense of background focus it had for what would be, in effect, the inclusion of a bunch of Prestige Classes. Less mystery, less symbolism and just a bunch of power fantasy to replace it with. I don\u2019t buy the crap about \u2018misinterpretation' of the Book of Nod either - it actually lists the 13 Clans by name.<br /> <br /> If whoever mentioned that the Clan/Bloodline confusion could just be unspecific marketing talk, then maybe that is it. If so, some of the other justifications here will look silly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You mean like the prior editions, when we got 'the fleshcrafters because Necroscope was cool and freaky or the Clan of Snakes But Through Thulsa-Doom Conan Lens'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T14:40:05-08:00","id":1425244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425209#post1425209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the number &amp;quot;13&amp;quot; is not a silly symbolism already? What else, was the Third Generation embraced on the Halloween night, or Friday 13?</div> </div> </div> </div>No it\u2019s not for the reasons already pointed out on this thread. The original writers made 13 a significant number in the game, not me, and its biblical/occult references lends atmosphere to the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T14:40:17-08:00","id":1425245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425099#post1425099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But my point is that it's just a line in a press release (and some related chatter online). We shouldn't extrapolate that to mean that the Salubri have been elevated to clan status just yet.<br /> <br /> Press releases are for journalists as much as players. A journo who doesn't know VTM won't care that the Salubri are really a bloodline. And it's easier to say '3 new clans' than '2 new clans and 1 bloodline'.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also repeated the announcement video on the WoD YouTube channel, as well as Outstar's interview with Justin Achilli. I haven't even seen the press release.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T14:49:38-08:00","id":1425248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425189#post1425189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If whoever mentioned that the Clan/Bloodline confusion could just be unspecific marketing talk, then maybe that is it. If so, some of the other justifications here will look silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Book of Nod is not and really shouldn't be treated as a factual guide to Kindred history. It has a lot of bits that are ambiguous, clearly not true, or at least self-aggrandizing.<br /> <br /> Here's Justin Achilli calling the Salubri a clan: <a href=\"https://youtu.be/T-C1bj0rZPM?t=407\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/T-C1bj0rZPM?t=407</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T15:27:07-08:00","id":1425255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425248#post1425248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Book of Nod is not and really shouldn't be treated as a factual guide to Kindred history. It has a lot of bits that are ambiguous, clearly not true, or at least self-aggrandizing.<br /> <br /> Here's Justin Achilli calling the Salubri a clan: <a href=\"https://youtu.be/T-C1bj0rZPM?t=407\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/T-C1bj0rZPM?t=407</a></div> </div> </div> </div>There is no \u2018factual guide\u2019 to a fictional gameworld, but if the directional choice is to ignore previous symbolism, without any reason given, then the game loses atmosphere accordingly. I mean the logical extension of your argument is that the Book of Nod as a reference is now redundant in the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 11-20-2020, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T15:36:08-08:00","id":1425257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425255#post1425255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no \u2018factual guide\u2019 to a fictional gameworld, but if the directional choice is to ignore previous symbolism, without any reason given, then the game loses atmosphere accordingly. I mean the logical extension of your argument is that the Book of Nod as a reference is now redundant in the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire basis of your argument for 13 clans is that the Book of Nod is factual in the setting. Don't quibble over semantics now.<br /> <br /> The logical extension of my argument is that all in-character text is automatically suspicious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T15:45:30-08:00","id":1425258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425257#post1425257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The entire basis of your argument for 13 clans is that the Book of Nod is factual in the setting. Don't quibble over semantics now.<br /> <br /> The logical extension of my argument is that all in-character text is automatically suspicious.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it is not at all. The basis of my argument is that the game has always utilised symbolism like Nod, the number 13 and other Biblical/occult references to create a particular atmosphere. To chuck them out on a whim in a cavalier sense, without any reason given, puts the atmosphere that has served the game almost 30 years at risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T15:54:59-08:00","id":1425261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425258#post1425258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No it is not at all. The basis of my argument is that the game has always utilised symbolism like Nod, the number 13 and other Biblical/occult references to create a particular atmosphere. To chuck them out on a whim in a cavalier sense, without a reason given, puts the atmosphere that has served the game almost 30 years at risk.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't, though. If your argument isn't there should be 13 clans and supported with the Book of Nod saying there are 13 clans as you have said repeatedly, then you should state what you actually mean more clearly without leaning so much on the Book of Nod. The list of other occurrences of 13 in culture doesn't really build a strong argument that this particular thing should always be 13.<br /> <br /> And maybe not call other people &quot;silly.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T16:55:38-08:00","id":1425268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425261#post1425261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't, though. If your argument isn't there should be 13 clans and supported with the Book of Nod saying there are 13 clans as you have said repeatedly, then you should state what you actually mean more clearly without leaning so much on the Book of Nod. The list of other occurrences of 13 in culture doesn't really build a strong argument that this particular thing should always be 13.<br /> <br /> And maybe not call other people &quot;silly.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>What I have argued is perfectly clear and certainly doesn\u2019t deserve having straw man arguments lobbed in return. At no point ever did I start arguing about \u2018facts\u2019 in the Book of Nod. I have consistently referred to the lore presented in it as being fundamental to the atmosphere of the game. The arguments you are presenting right now are silly. If you don\u2019t appreciate the symbolism that was crafted into the original Vampire game, or the biblical/occult references it has then that is your issue, but they have always been with the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 11-20-2020, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T17:11:01-08:00","id":1425272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425244#post1425244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No it\u2019s not for the reasons already pointed out on this thread. The original writers made 13 a significant number in the game, not me, and its biblical/occult references lends atmosphere to the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For the goth teens in the 90s, maybe. Now, it would only make people laugh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T17:19:29-08:00","id":1425275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425268#post1425268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I have argued is perfectly clear and certainly doesn\u2019t deserve having straw man arguments lobbed in return. At no point ever did I start arguing about \u2018facts\u2019 in the Book of Nod. I have consistently referred to the lore presented in it as being fundamental to the atmosphere of the game. The arguments you are presenting right now are silly. If you don\u2019t appreciate the symbolism that was crafted into the original Vampire game, or the biblical/occult references it has then that is your issue, but they have always been with the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fundamental, atmosphere, written in canon... unshakable and immovable foundations of the game.. <br /> in the meantime, the very creators of the game are freely toying around with new ideas, ready to reinvigorate the overcrowded, dusty old lore with them. Doing the right thing as adult, mature creators would do instead of guarding the old truths as something sacred and untouchable. I understand nostalgia is a hell of a drug, but c'mon. Time to move on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T17:53:20-08:00","id":1425285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425272#post1425272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the goth teens in the 90s, maybe. Now, it would only make people laugh.</div> </div> </div> </div>The same references can be found in the latest edition of the game, released just a couple of years ago. Nice bit of disparagement over the origins of the game though. We\u2019re you actually born in the 1990s, may I ask?<br /> <br /> And in response to your second post, the current development team were not actually the original creators, and your aren\u2019t their spokesperson. Like I say, if they turn around in a couple of weeks and say something that reestablishes 13 Clans again, all these arguments will look silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 11-21-2020, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T17:57:17-08:00","id":1425286,"title":"","content":"I purchased Vampire first edition in 1991, and started playing almost immediately. I did VLARP for several years. I ran and played in several tabletop chronicles.<br /> <br /> I don't see any problem with rejuvenating the game with new ideas, new assumptions, new clans, and new takes on the old material.<br /> <br /> The excellent Vampire 20 material published over the past several years is intentionally meant to appeal to fans of any of the first three editions, they're not really the authority to appeal to for precedent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T18:02:18-08:00","id":1425287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425268#post1425268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I have argued is perfectly clear and certainly doesn\u2019t deserve having straw man arguments lobbed in return. At no point ever did I start arguing about \u2018facts\u2019 in the Book of Nod. I have consistently referred to the lore presented in it as being fundamental to the atmosphere of the game. The arguments you are presenting right now are silly. If you don\u2019t appreciate the symbolism that was crafted into the original Vampire game, or the biblical/occult references it has then that is your issue, but they have always been with the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you need me to track down every time you've cited the Book of Nod for 13 clans? If the Book of Nod's not a factual reference to Cainite history, and only the symbolism is important, I would say that there's a lot more to the book's symbolism than the number 13.<br /> <br /> My arguments aren't silly - I just don't feel any particular allegiance to a number, nor do I think contradicting that number will lead to dogs and cats living together in the streets. It'll be fine. A silly argument is when you try to refer to a piece of fiction as justification for the fiction existing in that form. It's circular, and also weird. Setting aside the WoD and speaking generally, how do you kill a vampire? The answer to that is exactly the same as the answer to &quot;why must there be 13 clans?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T18:36:21-08:00","id":1425291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425286#post1425286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I purchased Vampire first edition in 1991, and started playing almost immediately. I did VLARP for several years. I ran and played in several tabletop chronicles.<br /> <br /> I don't see any problem with rejuvenating the game with new ideas, new assumptions, new clans, and new takes on the old material.<br /> <br /> The excellent Vampire 20 material published over the past several years is intentionally meant to appeal to fans of any of the first three editions, they're not really the authority to appeal to for precedent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t really see how it is rejuvenating anything. The Salubri were already well established - they were just presented as a Bloodline having a backstory as a deposed Clan. <br /> <br /> You don\u2019t need to track down anything about the Book of Nod, merely acknowledge that nobody is arguing it has \u2018factual content\u2019. It is a reference in the game that has always been present, and has been used since V1 as a means of presenting game lore. 13 Clans has always been present too, as a reference point, including V5 that states this throughout.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T19:28:34-08:00","id":1425298,"title":"","content":"Well, TO ME, even if they promote Salubri to Clan, I would consider the existence of only 13 clans still... Because Tremere is not a Clan. Only a half-assed Tzimisce bloodlines or trashy fallen mages... They don't even have a antediluvian. Lmaooooooo<br /> <br /> Death to all Tremeres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T20:22:58-08:00","id":1425308,"title":"","content":"Nah, there are 14 clans. It's just that three of them have no Antediluvian and are significantly reduced in numbers.<br /> <br /> There were 15, but then the Giovanni and the leftover Cappadocians had to become the same clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 11-20-2020, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T20:26:42-08:00","id":1425309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425291#post1425291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t really see how it is rejuvenating anything. The Salubri were already well established - they were just presented as a Bloodline having a backstory as a deposed Clan.<br /> <br /> You don\u2019t need to track down anything about the Book of Nod, merely acknowledge that nobody is arguing it has \u2018factual content\u2019. It is a reference in the game that has always been present, and has been used since V1 as a means of presenting game lore. 13 Clans has always been present too, as a reference point, including V5 that states this throughout.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't mean the Salubri specifically. One of the good things about V5 was that it was an attempt to bring Vampire: The Masquerade up to modern RPG standards, as they've evolved considerably since Revised. That is, an attempt to rejuvenate the game line. It's perfectly fine to assess the game as it existed then and exists in V20, bring forward the good stuff, and add more good stuff. Since, as you keep correctly pointing out, it's a fictional setting, that means the fiction can evolve over time, change over time, even be retconned over time. I'm not sure why you ascribe such a rigid metaphysics to it while also acknowledging it's fiction and thus malleable, but that's your prerogative.<br /> <br /> In-game lore often means in-game facts. Things that are facts within the setting itself. You're asserting that 13 clans is a mandatory fact of the setting. You can have facts about fictional settings. Obviously they're fictional facts because it's not real and vampires don't exist. The Book of Nod is not infallible or one hundred percent accurate within the setting. Anything in it could turn out to be wrong - in V5, it's clear that Gehenna didn't turn out as the prophecies stated, after all.<br /> <br /> I meant track down every time you've appealed to the Book of Nod to make factual assertions about the setting. Right now all I see is flying goalposts, so maybe this is as good a place as any to end this discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 11-20-2020, 11:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T22:35:49-08:00","id":1425317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425309#post1425309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't mean the Salubri specifically. One of the good things about V5 was that it was an attempt to bring Vampire: The Masquerade up to modern RPG standards, as they've evolved considerably since Revised. That is, an attempt to rejuvenate the game line. It's perfectly fine to assess the game as it existed then and exists in V20, bring forward the good stuff, and add more good stuff. Since, as you keep correctly pointing out, it's a fictional setting, that means the fiction can evolve over time, change over time, even be retconned over time. I'm not sure why you ascribe such a rigid metaphysics to it while also acknowledging it's fiction and thus malleable, but that's your prerogative.<br /> <br /> In-game lore often means in-game facts. Things that are facts within the setting itself. You're asserting that 13 clans is a mandatory fact of the setting. You can have facts about fictional settings. Obviously they're fictional facts because it's not real and vampires don't exist. The Book of Nod is not infallible or one hundred percent accurate within the setting. Anything in it could turn out to be wrong - in V5, it's clear that Gehenna didn't turn out as the prophecies stated, after all.<br /> <br /> I meant track down every time you've appealed to the Book of Nod to make factual assertions about the setting. Right now all I see is flying goalposts, so maybe this is as good a place as any to end this discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The last comment is factually wrong. I have merely pointed out to somebody arguing that the Book of Nod could be interpreted as suggesting 30 Clans - that <i>in fact</i> it mentions the 13 Clans by name, so there is no issue of interpretation. That is not asserting that the Book of Nod is factual itself - it is a work of fiction in reality and a book of myth in the setting. It\u2019s a strawman argument to suggest that I said anything otherwise, because I didn't.<br /> <br /> In game lore is just that - it is not a list of 'facts'. However, I am saying that the game\u2019s symbolism has always made use of the same symbolism contained in things like the number 13, and indeed the Book of Hod, as Biblical references or occult references. The game lore creates its atmosphere by doing so. If you contradict that lore, you alter the atmosphere accordingly and in my view that is detrimental to the game. That is it. That is my argument - everything else is a misrepresentation of my statements.<br /> <br /> And yes, V5 introduced a lot of excellent things into the game that rejuvenated the line. One thing they kept, however, was 13 Clans of Vampire - explicitly stated in the text. So has all the other editions. They were right to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 11-21-2020, 01:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T02:02:03-08:00","id":1425331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425309#post1425309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the good things about V5 was that it was an attempt to bring Vampire: The Masquerade up to modern RPG standards, as they've evolved considerably since Revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>RPG standards: you say evolved, i say fallen to ruin. The only &quot;new&quot; rpg that's impressed me in the past decade was Pathfinder, because it was a cleaned up version of a good system. Not a slash and burn or reinventing the wheel to have three points so the ride is much less smooth.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T02:07:58-08:00","id":1425333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425331#post1425331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> RPG standards: you say evolved, i say fallen to ruin. The only &quot;new&quot; rpg that's impressed me in the past decade was Pathfinder, because it was a cleaned up version of a good system. Not a slash and burn or reinventing the wheel to have three points so the ride is much less smooth.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The past decade has produced better RPGs than anyone in the 90s had ever dreamt of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T02:40:23-08:00","id":1425335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425333#post1425333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The past decade has produced better RPGs than anyone in the 90s had ever dreamt of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Y'know a couple of years ago, my group spent six months trying out new games at our weekly sessions. None of them were good enough to make us want to try them long term, and we just stuck to our 90's rpgs. The modern way seems to be at the same time gimicky faff while removing as much crunch as possible. Dull and frustrating to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T02:51:52-08:00","id":1425336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425335#post1425335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Y'know a couple of years ago, my group spent six months trying out new games at our weekly sessions. None of them were good enough to make us want to try them long term, and we just stuck to our 90's rpgs. The modern way seems to be at the same time gimicky faff while removing as much crunch as possible. Dull and frustrating to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't account for your group's tastes. I've only played RPGs since 1980 and the stuff that came out in the 2010s took RPGs to more interesting, more imaginative, and more flexible places. Give me Monsterhearts over the 90s any day.<br /> <br /> Also, crunch is not something to universally aspire to.<br /> <br /> Finally, I'll always love V:tM, regardless of era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 11-21-2020, 06:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T04:16:16-08:00","id":1425340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425285#post1425285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tge same references can be found in the latest edition of the game, released just a couple of years ago. Nice bit of disparagement over the origins of the game though. We\u2019re you actually born in the 1990s, may I ask?<br /> <br /> And in response to your second post, the current development team were not actually the original creators, and your aren\u2019t their spokesperson. Like I say, if they turn around in a couple of weeks and say something that reestablishes 13 Clans again, all these arguments will look silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I first encountered WoD/VtM in 2004, I was both fascinated by the maturity and grittiness of the setting compared to everything else RPG I've encountered, and then imagine my amusement when I found out that people thought having 13 (!) clan progenitors back thousands of years ago was a great idea which could lend to the narrative weight and atmosphere of the game. But then, I proceeded with reading on my native region, and laughed even harder. Having a Nosferatu Methuselah named Baba Yaga is somewhere near having 13 clans in terms of seriousness and atmosphere. To be honest, I don't think VtM origin was a fairy tale.<br /> <br /> Origins of the game are not a sacred cow to be guarded and worshipped at all costs, especially since the game grew much larger than it's original audience in the 90s. It all sounds like 'well well don't upset your grandma with your crazy progressive ideas now'.<br /> <br /> I'm not their spokeperson but it looks like I'm the only one who bothered checking on their opinion on the matter and staying in touch with their media accoutns to know of their ideas and suggestions on the setting development.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T04:58:33-08:00","id":1425343,"title":"","content":"DnD 5e is a good modern game. It's very streamlined. Yet I completely believe I'm playing an edition of DnD with it. <br /> <br /> 5e... what about this game is modern, other than how 'current' it is with events and how much it wears it's politics on it's sleeve? (note: It's good that a game is political, it's not good that the game presents it's political ideas so fucking badly that people want to dissociate it. A Bad argument is worse than no argument, and V5 is filled with bad arguments) <br /> The Game hasn't been streamlined, or made better, or otherwise improved. It's just <i>Different. </i>It's very different, and most compelling arguments would say it's worse. <br /> <br /> Also, I don't know about you guys, but the original game is just... genius. Secretly genius. Some of it's deliberate, some of it's accidental, but it's genius. I've never seen such a compelling setting before. Maybe I've got the benefit of hindsight because I get to look back on it and avoid products like <i>Gypsies</i> but the OG makers of the setting must've been IRL wizards or something. There's just so much unstated that just comes together and just... works. It's difficult to fully articulate how... hollistic they wrote everything. It's got me into all sorts of esoteric stuff as a result (please help me, I have a problem, it's only a matter of time till I find the real Tremere) The latest edition seems to be picking things apart without care or understanding for the greater whole. A good portion of changes seem to be &quot;I personally don't like this faction so I'll change them more to my liking&quot; and that's... how you make the setting feel artificial. V5 seems more like a 'just a game' than ever before. DnD 5e by contrast feels more organic with it's reduced and simplified mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T05:28:47-08:00","id":1425351,"title":"","content":"D&amp;D is largely its own thing on an entirely different level from the rest of the industry, and 5e was the result of fans wanting it to be like it was in 3e all over again. The rest of the industry is a bit separated from the kinds of assumptions and sensibilities that inform D&amp;D's design. 4e wasn't a bad game, but it wasn't the D&amp;D everyone wanted to play, and WotC followed the money.<br /> <br /> And yes the original Vampire was great for its time, outsold AD&amp;D for a year or so, before WotC purchased TSR, and continues to hold some popularity. Given the success of the V20 line, Paradox bringing V5 about was probably a very good move. It doesn't feel like &quot;just a game,&quot; and it still benefits from past lore, even if not slavishly held to it (thankfully).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T05:31:50-08:00","id":1425352,"title":"","content":"The amount of time, effort and, let's be honest, at times even talent some people put into pounding on V5 in their every single post is simply anecdotal at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T05:47:49-08:00","id":1425355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425336#post1425336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't account for your group's tastes. I've only played RPGs since 1980 and the stuff that came out in the 2010s took RPGs to more interesting, more imaginative, and more flexible places. Give me <b><i>Monsterhearts</i></b> over the 90s any day.<br /> <br /> Also, crunch is not something to universally aspire to.<br /> <br /> Finally, I'll always love V:tM, regardless of era.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sweet Budda, it's like weaponised cringe...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T06:59:22-08:00","id":1425359,"title":"","content":"The way I feel about VTM is first edition was mind blowing and addictive, second edition cleaned up some rules but added A LOT of power creep, revised was both interesting and a turn off on a lot of levels, but some of the people I played with LOVED it even if I thought it was too much of a box, when it was nuked from orbit to bring us Requiem everyone I know stopped buying new books, it wasn't VTM. I think the 20th books are great and I use the PDF's. If they had put the 20th books in stores I would own them. 5th edition like Requiem isn't VTM to me, I haven't spent a dime on it despite flirting with the idea of getting CbN just to read. I don't mind the second inquisition, I nuked the Tremere years ago, Making Anarchs a real thing is fine just not at the expense of the Sabbat if you want to keep a large portion of your fanbase.<br /> <br /> I do however find the massive rule changes so off putting even with the free companion I signed up for I can't see how it could possibly fix what has been broken in my eyes. I remain hopeful for 6th edition but news of coming changes has got me checking the site several times a day to read posts. Maybe it's just because we don't get into lots of combat all the time we just don't find soak rolls so time consuming. I would love new books to read and hopefully get inspired to take things from, but if they don't figure out how to undo most of the game altering changes it just seems like too much work I will have to do converting things to pay money for.<br /> <br /> Best case? I'm hoping the Companion rules errata will be sweeping, bringing back virtues roads blood pools, while dropping things like hunger and touch stones, the promise to soon fix disciplines that were dramatically changed and the first fifth edition book I buy --- the core rule book 5.5... I doubt this will happen but I'm looking forward to my free Companion PDF and seeing just how they try to bring me back.<br /> <br /> The biggest problem with &quot;modernizing&quot; games to be the cool new thing is I still have my basic D&amp;D and AD&amp;D books and my friends are happy to play them and not spend a small fortune. If I was still a big D&amp;D player I would no doubt have some third and fifth edition modules, some new PH and DM's Guides, maybe a bunch of MM's, maybe I switch all in on fifth edition I hear it's so wonderful. I played 4th edition D&amp;D at a comic book shop because they were trying to convince people to buy it. It wasn't D&amp;D and I would never have bought any of it. Boy I hope the coming changes make me good with fifth edition VTM but I have my doubts. At least the announcement has given me hours of fun reading message boards I had been paying little attention to for awhile now if nothing else.<br /> <br /> What a rambling post I just wrote...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T11:51:47-08:00","id":1425385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425340#post1425340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When I first encountered WoD/VtM in 2004, I was both fascinated by the maturity and grittiness of the setting compared to everything else RPG I've encountered, and then imagine my amusement when I found out that people thought having 13 (!) clan progenitors back thousands of years ago was a great idea which could lend to the narrative weight and atmosphere of the game. But then, I proceeded with reading on my native region, and laughed even harder. Having a Nosferatu Methuselah named Baba Yaga is somewhere near having 13 clans in terms of seriousness and atmosphere. To be honest, I don't think VtM origin was a fairy tale.<br /> <br /> Origins of the game are not a sacred cow to be guarded and worshipped at all costs, especially since the game grew much larger than it's original audience in the 90s. It all sounds like 'well well don't upset your grandma with your crazy progressive ideas now'.<br /> <br /> I'm not their spokeperson but it looks like I'm the only one who bothered checking on their opinion on the matter and staying in touch with their media accoutns to know of their ideas and suggestions on the setting development.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn\u2019t look like you check out others opinions as much as you are projecting your own in this instance. You haven\u2019t actually answered the point that the latest version of Vampire actually, explicitly, refers to 13 Clans still. Moreover, the origins of the game, generally, are still canon - you still have the same original Clans named in the core game, and it is not as if the Salubri, Ravnos or Tzmisce are new either. The simple fact here is that is that the current developers have simply redeveloped what was already existing in the 1990s, but just haven\u2019t explained how there has come to be 14 Clans rather than 13 Clans that is currently and historically written in the game. They may well do so in the descriptions and explanations in the Companion. If you actually find the number 13 or integrating real world folk lore like Baba Yaga into the game\u2019s background as a source of amusement, then I\u2019m not entirely sure where your humour is coming from on the matter. Nevertheless, real world cultures and religions do lend historical narratives that people relate to, and Vampire as a game sources these things heavily.<br /> <br /> I think the main strength of Vampire, as a game, is the effectiveness that it creates its atmosphere - and the current version of the game still refers to itself as \u2018gothic\u2019, incidentally, if that also amuses you still. The use of symbolism in its background detail lends to that atmosphere, as attested to the fact that the whole game is based around the supernatural existence of Vampires (along with werewolves, ghosts, etc). This is all based on folklore and romantic symbolism, intermixed with contemporary culture. If you change aspects of it, without explanation or just for some misguided notion of \u2019sacred cows', you risk affecting that atmosphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 11-21-2020, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T12:14:50-08:00","id":1425387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425385#post1425385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn\u2019t look like you check out others opinions as much as you are projecting your own in this instance. You haven\u2019t actually answered the point that the latest version of Vampire actually, explicitly, refers to 13 Clans still. Moreover, the origins of the game, generally, are still canon - you still have the same Clans named, and it is not as if the Salubri, Ravnos or Tzmisce are new either. The simple fact here is that is that the current developers have simply redeveloped what was already existing in the 1990s, but haven\u2019t explained how there has come to be 14 Clans rather than 13 Clans that is currently and historically written in the game. They may well do so in the descriptions and explanations in the Companion. If you actually find the number 13 or integrating real world folk lore like Baba Yaga into the game\u2019s background as a source of amusement, then I\u2019m not entirely sure where your humour is coming from on the matter. Nevertheless, real world cultures and religions do lend historical narratives that people relate to, and Vampire as a game sources these things heavily. I think the main strength of Vampire, as a game, is the effectiveness that it creates its atmosphere - and the current version of the game still refers to itself as \u2018gothic\u2019, incidentally, if that also amuses you still. The use of symbolism in its background detail lends to that atmosphere. If you change aspects of it, without explanation or just for some misguided notion of \u2019sacred cows', you risk affecting that atmosphere.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> did you take off your monocle to write all that stuff or not, that's what really bothers me here.<br /> <br /> on a more serious note, stop trying to elevate the stupidly, positively juvenile origins of the game to some perceived heights only you and the chosen few of the players are supposedly entitled to encompass and fully understand. <br /> real world folk lore baba yaga is the simplest fairy tale out here, akin to paul banyan or robin hood. silly, funny, stupid and low key. the moment you stop aggrandising stuff like that you'll get my point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T12:36:22-08:00","id":1425388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425387#post1425387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> did you take off your monocle to write all that stuff or not, that's what really bothers me here.<br /> <br /> on a more serious note, stop trying to elevate the stupidly, positively juvenile origins of the game to some perceived heights only you and the chosen few of the players are supposedly entitled to encompass and fully understand.<br /> real world folk lore baba yaga is the simplest fairy tale out here, akin to paul banyan or robin hood. silly, funny, stupid and low key. the moment you stop aggrandising stuff like that you'll get my point.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what bothers you is that somebody has a different opinion to yourself.<br /> <br /> On a more serious note (how could it be less serious?), your own attitude to the origins of the game is juvenile. We can see that in the way in which you choose to talk in pejorative terms about it, name calling the people who originally created it and the people who played it. All of which eventuated in the game we have today, that apparently you are a fan of - although I am not sure why, going on all your comments here.<br /> <br /> Baba Yaga has been used as a boogeyman figure in all sorts of media references and, whether you think it is silly or not, they have integrated into the WoD lore also. Maybe, the moment you start appreciating that your own views aren\u2019t really that important, then we might have a dialogue that doesn\u2019t resemble your own kindergarten experiences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 11-21-2020, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T22:10:26-08:00","id":1425453,"title":"","content":"Damn all this argument over number 13... lol","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T22:13:53-08:00","id":1425454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425453#post1425453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn all this argument over number 13... lol</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it takes two (or more) to tango, but for me, it is part of the game world that has always established 13 Clans. What people choose to read into that is up to them, I guess, but I like the symbolism and it was obviously something that each edition has felt it needed to establish as part of its lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T22:36:50-08:00","id":1425457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425453#post1425453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn all this argument over number 13... lol</div> </div> </div> </div>It was over but then he had to insult people over it out of the blue","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T22:43:25-08:00","id":1425459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425457#post1425457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was over but then he had to insult people over it out of the blue</div> </div> </div> </div>If you were offended by anything then I apologize, but I thought the arguments against having 13 Clans got silly, especially because there hasn\u2019t been any official statement on the matter. And I\u2019m not the person who thought it sensible to start attacking 90s goths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T22:43:50-08:00","id":1425460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425352#post1425352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The amount of time, effort and, let's be honest, at times even talent some people put into pounding on V5 in their every single post is simply anecdotal at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do admit it's kind of weird given that edition warring is frowned upon here.<br /> <br /> I'm just glad I could find stuff in V5 to like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T22:45:58-08:00","id":1425461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425459#post1425459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you were offended by anything then I apologize, but I thought the arguments against having 13 Clans got silly, especially because there hasn\u2019t been any official statement on the matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not really arguments against 13 clans, more like arguments that having 14 would be fine.<br /> <br /> I'm fine either way. If they bring back the Bloodline language, that'll be great and consistent. If they decide everything's a clan, that'd be weird but okay. If they're like well the Salubri are a clan because they were before, that's fine too. I'm not so much committed to a specific outcome as I am to seeing what we get in the Companion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T22:46:14-08:00","id":1425462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425336#post1425336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't account for your group's tastes. I've only played RPGs since 1980 and the stuff that came out in the 2010s took RPGs to more interesting, more imaginative, and more flexible places. Give me Monsterhearts over the 90s any day.<br /> <br /> Also, crunch is not something to universally aspire to.<br /> <br /> Finally, I'll always love V:tM, regardless of era.</div> </div> </div> </div>Crunch does, I find correlate fairly well with playability , fun, and quality. The better and more detailed the crunch, the better and more detailed the story and setting tend to be, the more 'streamlined' the rules, the less coherent and fun the setting. Not universally true, but more crunch more better is a decent rule of thumb for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T22:48:21-08:00","id":1425463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425461#post1425461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're not really arguments against 13 clans, more like arguments that having 14 would be fine.<br /> <br /> I'm fine either way. If they bring back the Bloodline language, that'll be great and consistent. If they decide everything's a clan, that'd be weird but okay. If they're like well the Salubri are a clan because they were before, that's fine too. I'm not so much committed to a specific outcome as I am to seeing what we get in the Companion.</div> </div> </div> </div>No they weren\u2019t. They were arguments trying to belittle the symbolism used in every edition, including V5, that made a point of there being 13 Clans. They were silly because of it. I await and see what the official explanation about Clans/Bloodline distinctions will be, but the canon has always had 13 Clans. This is not something that is insignificant in the game, and liking them does not make somebody a 90s Goth or a barrier towards the games\u2019 innovation - so claiming these things has not been helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 11-22-2020, 01:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T23:34:04-08:00","id":1425466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425463#post1425463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No they weren\u2019t. They were arguments trying to belittle the symbolism used in every edition, including V5, that made a point of there being 13 Clans. They were silly because of it. I await and see what the official explanation about Clans/Bloodline distinctions will be, but the canon has always had 13 Clans. This is not something that is insignificant in the game, and liking them does not make somebody a 90s Goth or a barrier towards the games\u2019 innovation - so claiming these things has not been helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>While 13 is very symbolic, the fact is that multiple clans exist now beyond the 13 because of Antediluvians being diablerized.<br /> <br /> * True Brujah<br /> * Salubri<br /> * Cappadocians<br /> <br /> There's also 14 Antediluvians because Tremere ascended to 3rd generation after losing his body and performing a mass sacrifice of the Tremere Antitribu.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T23:43:23-08:00","id":1425467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425466#post1425466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While 13 is very symbolic, the fact is that multiple clans exist now beyond the 13 because of Antediluvians being diablerized.<br /> <br /> * True Brujah<br /> * Salubri<br /> * Cappadocians<br /> <br /> There's also 14 Antediluvians because Tremere ascended to 3rd generation after losing his body and performing a mass sacrifice of the Tremere Antitribu.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I know that, but the point was they kept to the 13 Clan motif by establishing that these were the result of Diablerie and succession. All these are 'ex-Clans' because of it - that is what I am getting at. The power of the Tremere backstory, for example, lies in the fact that they <i>stole</i> the status of one of the 13 Clans, who are now relegated to being merely a (rare) Bloodline.<br /> <br /> And actually, you can help me with this because I am only slowly reading through Cults of the Blood Gods right now, but what is the relationship/status of the Cappadocians/Giovanni/Hecata Clan? When did one become the other and how?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 11-22-2020, 02:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T23:45:41-08:00","id":1425468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425463#post1425463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No they weren\u2019t. They were arguments trying to belittle the symbolism used in every edition, including V5, that made a point of there being 13 Clans. They were silly because of it. I await and see what the official explanation about Clans/Bloodline distinctions will be, but the canon has always had 13 Clans. This is not something that is insignificant in the game, and liking them does not make somebody a 90s Goth or a barrier towards the games\u2019 innovation - so claiming these things has not been helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>The arguments aren't silly, and no the belittling didn't happen. What happened was people said that 13 was just a number and it's okay to depart from that symbolism, and then you listed several unrelated 13s as examples of cultural importance of 13, but &quot;They can have more if they want&quot; isn't silly, nor was my analogy about planets and dwarf planets, nor was anything else.<br /> <br /> But continually bringing it back to calling disagreements silly is precisely the problem I referred to previously.<br /> <br /> I think we've established where we stand on this, and further discussion won't go anywhere new. I don't think your reasons are silly, and I don't think 13 clans are silly. I'm just chill with having 13 or 14 or 15 or 16 or 12 or whatever. This one setting feature is not that important to me. I don't think it's central to Vampire's identity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 11-22-2020, 03:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T23:50:51-08:00","id":1425469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425462#post1425462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Crunch does, I find correlate fairly well with playability , fun, and quality. The better and more detailed the crunch, the better and more detailed the story and setting tend to be, the more 'streamlined' the rules, the less coherent and fun the setting. Not universally true, but more crunch more better is a decent rule of thumb for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone can prefer more or less crunch that's a personal matter, but my experience in running RPGs is that adding crunch has a tendency to put players off, whereas the fewer things between the players and what they want their characters to do, the more fun it's been for me. I had one player who simply did not click with the Mage combat rules and I had to do a flowchart for combat, and said player still needed help with combat.<br /> <br /> Also Fate can be as crunchy as you want. Dresden Files RPG vs. FAE Dresden Files RPG shows two ends of a spectrum in that regard. But overall, I want players to spend more time thinking about playing their characters than how many dice to roll in like 50 very specific different contexts.<br /> <br /> But also I love to roll multiple D10s and I'd even play Exalted again despite its heavy crunch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 11-22-2020, 03:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T00:05:19-08:00","id":1425471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425468#post1425468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The arguments aren't silly, and no the belittling didn't happen. What happened was people said that 13 was just a number and it's okay to depart from that symbolism, and then you listed several unrelated 13s as examples of cultural importance of 13, but &quot;They can have more if they want&quot; isn't silly, nor was my analogy about planets and dwarf planets, nor was anything else.<br /> <br /> But continually bringing it back to calling disagreements silly is precisely the problem I referred to previously.</div> </div> </div> </div>There has been arguments on this thread that have suggested that the Book of Nod could be interpreted as suggesting 30 clans (which it couldn\u2019t because they were all named in that book), that any reference to the Book of Nod should be dismissed because it wasn\u2019t \u201cfactual&quot; (even though this point was never argued), that any reference made in the game to 13 Clans or anything else were \u201claughable\u201d and liking the symbolism made you a &quot;90s Goth Teen\u201d. So, yes, these <i>were </i>silly arguments and belittling.<br /> <br /> And no, in the game lore <i>as it still stands, </i>13 is not just a number - it is explicitly how many Clans there are. It is part of the symbolism of the game as CTPhipps just pointed out - it is a self-evident truth that the writers of the game deliberately made \u201913' a motif in the game. There could be arguments as to why these things may have changed or be changeable as the game moves forward, and we have yet to see what the official line on the matter is, but to flat out deny it or claim that adjusting the number isn\u2019t significant in the game lore, <i>is</i> a silly argument regardless of whether it is important or not to you.<br /> <br /> I wasn\u2019t actually referring to your analogy about planets or dwarf planets when I pointed out about silly arguments. That wasn\u2019t silly per se, it was just a bad analogy for the reasons given before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 11-22-2020, 03:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T00:09:41-08:00","id":1425472,"title":"","content":"I edited to add more to that post and you should read it. I'm not going to continue this argument. I just ask that you stop trashing other people's opinions.<br /> <br /> You not understanding my arguments does not make them silly or nonsense. I took pains to insure they were explained as thoroughly as I could. I don't recall insulting you at any point although I apologize if I did.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T00:15:03-08:00","id":1425474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425472#post1425472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just ask that you stop trashing other people's opinions.</div> </div> </div> </div>You may be conflating my responses to other posters comments with your own, somewhat, so you might look into that. Yet trying to insinuate that somebody doesn\u2019t \u201cunderstand\u201d your arguments is also belittling, by the way, so you probably ought to take a note out of your own book too. I\u2019ve made it clear what arguments I thought were silly, and why. Take it or leave it - makes little difference to me at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T00:31:08-08:00","id":1425475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425474#post1425474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may be conflating my responses to other posters comments with your own, somewhat, so you might look into that. Yet trying to insinuate that somebody doesn\u2019t \u201cunderstand\u201d your arguments is also belittling, by the way, so you probably ought to take a note out of your own book too. I\u2019ve made it clear what arguments I thought were silly, and why. Take it or leave it - makes little difference to me at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>The analogy was fine and actually relevant. If you don't like the fact that categories aren't engraved in stone but rather defined by people I don't know what to say. That applies as much to planets as it does to species as it does to fiction genres as it does to role playing games as it does to groups within role playing games as it does to clans and bloodlines specifically. Whatever the criteria you establish, they can be changed if in the future as needed or in the case of fiction, as wanted. You may not like that, but it won't change the fact that it's true, or that this was what the analogy was meant to illustrate.<br /> <br /> Also, you referencing the Book of Nod naming 13 clans meaning there must be 13 clans is actually a claim that the Book of Nod is a factual document within the World of Darkness. This isn't the same as saying that it's a factual document in the real world. You were saying that the lore from the Book of Nod needs to define what's allowed within the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Anyway, you've convinced me. I really want to see 14+ official clans all existing at the same time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T00:47:04-08:00","id":1425478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425469#post1425469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anyone can prefer more or less crunch that's a personal matter, but my experience in running RPGs is that adding crunch has a tendency to put players off, whereas the fewer things between the players and what they want their characters to do, the more fun it's been for me. I had one player who simply did not click with the Mage combat rules and I had to do a flowchart for combat, and said player still needed help with combat.<br /> <br /> Also Fate can be as crunchy as you want. Dresden Files RPG vs. FAE Dresden Files RPG shows two ends of a spectrum in that regard. But overall, I want players to spend more time thinking about playing their characters than how many dice to roll in like 50 very specific different contexts.<br /> <br /> But also I love to roll multiple D10s and I'd even play Exalted again despite its heavy crunch.</div> </div> </div> </div>I played the Dresden files RPG in about 2013/14...once,the system was way to light and vague to be any fun, and that was the full FATE rules. <br /> <br /> Dark Heresy, Eclipse Phase, Warhammer fantasy, Pathfinder 1e etc are way more my level of detail, meaning previous editions of the WoD games we were using WoD combat, expanded social rules etc etc, when I was in a group that allowed that. But then It view rules as the skeleton the story hangs off, if the rules aren't robust the story falls apart, if the story isn't robust then nothing moves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 11-22-2020, 03:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T00:48:18-08:00","id":1425479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425475#post1425475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The analogy was fine and actually relevant. If you don't like the fact that categories aren't engraved in stone but rather defined by people I don't know what to say. That applies as much to planets as it does to species as it does to fiction genres as it does to role playing games as it does to groups within role playing games as it does to clans and bloodlines specifically. Whatever the criteria you establish, they can be changed if in the future as needed or in the case of fiction, as wanted. You may not like that, but it won't change the fact that it's true, or that this was what the analogy was meant to illustrate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t care. That conversation finished a while ago. You may have an opinion. I might have another. We agreed to disagree, so why bring it up again? You\u2019ve conflated the criticism of this with that of another poster, and now you are just obsessing over it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, you referencing the Book of Nod naming 13 clans meaning there must be 13 clans is actually a claim that the Book of Nod is a factual document within the World of Darkness. This isn't the same as saying that it's a factual document in the real world. You were saying that the lore from the Book of Nod needs to define what's allowed within the World of Darkness. </div> </div> </div>Wrong. The factual issue is that somebody argued that the Book of Nod could be interpreted as stating there were 30 Clans rather than 13. This was factually untrue because 13 Clans are literally named in it - and this is what I pointed out. This does not mean anybody is claiming that the Book of Nod is a factual document, in game or out of it. A classic strawman argument.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway, you've convinced me. I really want to see 14+ official clans all existing at the same time. </div> </div> </div>Great. You don\u2019t get to decide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 11-22-2020, 04:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T00:52:48-08:00","id":1425481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425478#post1425478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I played the Dresden files RPG in about 2013/14...once,the system was way to light and vague to be any fun, Dark Heresy, Eclipse Phase, Warhammer fantasy, Pathfinder 1e etc are way more my level of detail, meaning previous editions of the WoD games we were using WoD combat, expanded social rules etc etc, when I was in a group that allowed that. But then It view rules as the skeleton the story hangs off, if the rules aren't robust the story falls apart, if the story isn't robust then nothing moves.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's weird. I've never found that story needs crunchy rules or it falls apart. I've found some games' rules can actually force anticlimactic or other unsatisfying outcomes.<br /> <br /> Amber has some of the least crunchy rules ever written and is almost entirely handled narratively. It's been played for nearly three decades without a hitch, plus a new game using similar rules with a different setting was made as homage, and that gets played at AmberCon as well.<br /> <br /> PbtA and Fate both have a lot of games using their rules-light framework. There must be some reason people keep making them - maybe crunch isn't required after all and is a matter of personal preference.<br /> <br /> Also, the trend toward less crunch is good, actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T01:03:02-08:00","id":1425482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425481#post1425481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's weird. I've never found that story needs crunchy rules or it falls apart. I've found some games' rules can actually force anticlimactic or other unsatisfying outcomes.<br /> <br /> Amber has some of the least crunchy rules ever written and is almost entirely handled narratively. It's been played for nearly three decades without a hitch, plus a new game using similar rules with a different setting was made as homage, and that gets played at AmberCon as well.<br /> <br /> PbtA and Fate both have a lot of games using their rules-light framework. There must be some reason people keep making them - maybe crunch isn't required after all and is a matter of personal preference.<br /> <br /> Also, the trend toward less crunch is good, actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why, originally I said 'a decent rule of thumb for me' rules light systems do not work for me, the trend towards less crunch is saving me money I guess, because I buy less games knowing I won't enjoy them just from the description.. I gave Fate a chance, but didn't enjoy it and I love the Dresdenverse, but not having rules for things, having them be only narrative flourish... well I want crunch for HOW taking powerful slow strikes Vs quick counter punches,. How bombastic boasting Vs quiet menace, how roguishly charming Vs sly and seductive....for me without the rules under those differences, they become mushy and story suffers, but again that's for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T01:13:27-08:00","id":1425483,"title":"","content":"The thing is though the Storyteller system was simple as fuck though and didn't have any crunch at all; to mention in the first place since this discussion is centered around WoD in general. Just get a couple of d10 dice, set the difficulty via the ST or its static DC if noted via the game itself, and just roll. It didn't need &quot;streamlining&quot; since it was already easy as you could get in comparison to other systems. V5 &quot;streamlines&quot; (if you can call them that) weren't needed at all for the franchise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 11-22-2020, 05:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T01:39:15-08:00","id":1425485,"title":"","content":"RE-Storyteller system. <br /> -I agree, for the most part. The storyteller system was beautifully simple. However, it did have it's flaws. <br /> -An attack is dealt with in 3-4 rolls (Attack, Defence, Damage, Soak), rather than 1 or 2 (just &quot;Take half&quot; for Damage/Soak already)<br /> Character creation was pretty imbalanced, Rising XP costs heavily rewarded characters who started with stuff like 1/4/1 , 4/1/3, 4/1/5 , 10 willpower, 1/1/1 in disciplines, 5's in few backgrounds... I really don't like the way V5 does it, but they're clearly trying to adress something that's a problem. IMO we needed flat rates for experience, except for Disciplines which v5 did right with '2/1/0' <br /> <br /> RE-13 clans. <br /> I think it interests us so much because it's Trippy. A guy who overwhelmingly praises the most drastic, controversial changes to V5. Yet the prospect of a 14th clan phases him. I had some analogies in mind but... I'm not very good with those. I think if I was so adamant about the number of clans nobody'd really care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T01:39:51-08:00","id":1425486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425482#post1425482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is why, originally I said 'a decent rule of thumb for me' rules light systems do not work for me, the trend towards less crunch is saving me money I guess, because I buy less games knowing I won't enjoy them just from the description.. I gave Fate a chance, but didn't enjoy it and I love the Dresdenverse, but not having rules for things, having them be only narrative flourish... well I want crunch for HOW taking powerful slow strikes Vs quick counter punches,. How bombastic boasting Vs quiet menace, how roguishly charming Vs sly and seductive....for me without the rules under those differences, they become mushy and story suffers, but again that's for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's cool. Sorry got caught up in a different point.<br /> <br /> Mage 2 could be very crunchy in its day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T03:47:38-08:00","id":1425492,"title":"","content":"For the 13 Clans part: I think it could become a rather interesting Plot-point in V5.<br /> Lets do a little mindgame: Lets say, a Salubri Methuselah (5th or 4th gen) gets awakened by the whole Gehena-War thing (whatever it is). In a Ur-Shulgi style manner he brings back the Salubri to power and prominence (he could be a forgotten Healer, who looks at the 7 living Healers and calls BS to their tradition, or a warrior that unites the antitribu and the healers and so on). So now we have a rather strong clan Salubri that goes around calling itself a Clan. Since they were an OG Clan, they would be like 'we were there from the very start, do NOT question our position!&quot;.<br /> So now all the factions and sub-factions have to deal with that. The more secular part of the Camarilla could not give a shit about if its 13 or 14 Clans and especially the Ventrue (who are also somewhat weakened through the whole Convention of Prague thing) could see an Opportunity to weakend their &quot;best buddy&quot; rivals Tremere and get some Salubri back to the Cam ('well, they were an original clan, what can we do...*g*').<br /> The more religious parts of the Camarilla could call out the heresy of having 14 Clans and rip themselves apart over wich Clan has to go (possibly the Tremere, the Salubri or the Hecata).<br /> Same with the Anarch and the Sabbath. You would have some Tremere 'loyalists' in all Sects that would not support the Salubri, while others finaly get some sweet revenge on those Tremere fuckers (did someone say Gangrel?).<br /> So if you keep the whole what/who is a 'Clan' a little more vague in Meta, you can generate some sweet Plot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26305-takeochan","name":"TakeoChan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T03:52:39-08:00","id":1425493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425485#post1425485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RE-13 clans.<br /> I think it interests us so much because it's Trippy. A guy who overwhelmingly praises the most drastic, controversial changes to V5. Yet the prospect of a 14th clan phases him. I had some analogies in mind but... I'm not very good with those. I think if I was so adamant about the number of clans nobody'd really care.</div> </div> </div> </div>How I\u2019ve missed your contributions to any given debate about V5....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T04:01:32-08:00","id":1425494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TakeoChan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425492#post1425492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the 13 Clans part: I think it could become a rather interesting Plot-point in V5.<br /> Lets do a little mindgame: Lets say, a Salubri Methuselah (5th or 4th gen) gets awakened by the whole Gehena-War thing (whatever it is). In a Ur-Shulgi style manner he brings back the Salubri to power and prominence (he could be a forgotten Healer, who looks at the 7 living Healers and calls BS to their tradition, or a warrior that unites the antitribu and the healers and so on). So now we have a rather strong clan Salubri that goes around calling itself a Clan. Since they were an OG Clan, they would be like 'we were there from the very start, do NOT question our position!&quot;.<br /> So now all the factions and sub-factions have to deal with that. The more secular part of the Camarilla could not give a shit about if its 13 or 14 Clans and especially the Ventrue (who are also somewhat weakened through the whole Convention of Prague thing) could see an Opportunity to weakend their &quot;best buddy&quot; rivals Tremere and get some Salubri back to the Cam ('well, they were an original clan, what can we do...*g*').<br /> The more religious parts of the Camarilla could call out the heresy of having 14 Clans and rip themselves apart over wich Clan has to go (possibly the Tremere, the Salubri or the Hecata).<br /> Same with the Anarch and the Sabbath. You would have some Tremere 'loyalists' in all Sects that would not support the Salubri, while others finaly get some sweet revenge on those Tremere fuckers (did someone say Gangrel?).<br /> So if you keep the whole what/who is a 'Clan' a little more vague in Meta, you can generate some sweet Plot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see that happening as a plot device - but we would have to wait for what the developers choose to do, hence the need for an explanation. As it stands though, 14 Clans is incongruous with what has always been established in the game world before, and the symbolism remains significant enough to have it stated as such in the core rules. The re-emergence of the Salubri might well be a meta plot development moving forward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T05:17:10-08:00","id":1425498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425485#post1425485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had some analogies in mind but... I'm not very good with those.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like your analogies! <br /> <br /> Woman half naked to thaum. Vs. Woman naked to blood sorcery.<br /> <br /> Dick the size of a child to Blood Potency 5+.<br /> <br /> Lmao.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T05:19:57-08:00","id":1425499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425498#post1425498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Woman half naked to thaum. Vs. Woman naked to blood sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no memory of this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T06:31:15-08:00","id":1425503,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">I think it's about time to move on from the 13 clan argument or at least make a new thread. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T06:38:21-08:00","id":1425504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425388#post1425388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Baba Yaga has been used as a boogeyman figure in all sorts of media references and, whether you think it is silly or not, they have integrated into the WoD lore also.</div> </div> </div> </div>..and the WW went to great length in v20 to correct the damage things like integrating baba yaga as a literal blood goddess methuselah ruling over irl post soviet with an iron fist did to the image and reputation of the game and its authors in the eyes of post-Soviet WoD players. There was a long discussion and promises from WW to avoid things like hilarious, cringy, blatant oversimplification of regional folklore integration into WoD to happen to the regions they know little about, and to do better research going forward to avoid cheese like that.<br /> <br /> I really like that approach, and seeing self-appointed authority in the forums defends the position which was proven wrong years ago by a whole post soviet WoD community is a nice reminder why we all, players, STs, publishers and authors, should stay vigilant and not allow the mistakes of the old era become 'the foundations of the lore'.<br /> <br /> Getting back to the topic, I hope to see the same respectful and innovative approach from Renegade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T06:56:01-08:00","id":1425505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TakeoChan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425492#post1425492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the 13 Clans part: I think it could become a rather interesting Plot-point in V5.<br /> Lets do a little mindgame: Lets say, a Salubri Methuselah (5th or 4th gen) gets awakened by the whole Gehena-War thing (whatever it is). In a Ur-Shulgi style manner he brings back the Salubri to power and prominence (he could be a forgotten Healer, who looks at the 7 living Healers and calls BS to their tradition, or a warrior that unites the antitribu and the healers and so on). So now we have a rather strong clan Salubri that goes around calling itself a Clan. Since they were an OG Clan, they would be like 'we were there from the very start, do NOT question our position!&quot;.<br /> So now all the factions and sub-factions have to deal with that. The more secular part of the Camarilla could not give a shit about if its 13 or 14 Clans and especially the Ventrue (who are also somewhat weakened through the whole Convention of Prague thing) could see an Opportunity to weakend their &quot;best buddy&quot; rivals Tremere and get some Salubri back to the Cam ('well, they were an original clan, what can we do...*g*').<br /> The more religious parts of the Camarilla could call out the heresy of having 14 Clans and rip themselves apart over wich Clan has to go (possibly the Tremere, the Salubri or the Hecata).<br /> Same with the Anarch and the Sabbath. You would have some Tremere 'loyalists' in all Sects that would not support the Salubri, while others finaly get some sweet revenge on those Tremere fuckers (did someone say Gangrel?).<br /> So if you keep the whole what/who is a 'Clan' a little more vague in Meta, you can generate some sweet Plot.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like the way you think, I wonder how many city's would have the Tremere locked in their house scared to come out and be eaten by a resurgent Clan Salubri. HokusPokus wont stop a broadsword from removing your head as you make your way to the local Elysium gathering. Political power means little to Sabbat rules of warfare, or lack there of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T07:02:37-08:00","id":1425506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425504#post1425504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ..and the WW went to great length in v20 to correct the damage things like integrating baba yaga as a literal blood goddess methuselah ruling over irl post soviet with an iron fist did to the image and reputation of the game and its authors in the eyes of post-Soviet WoD players. There was a long discussion and promises from WW to avoid things like hilarious, cringy, blatant oversimplification of regional folklore integration into WoD to happen to the regions they know little about, and to do better research going forward to avoid cheese like that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Asserting things on the internet doesn't make them real.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T07:15:27-08:00","id":1425509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425506#post1425506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Asserting things on the internet doesn't make them real.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can reach out for comment to Natalie Manzurenko, the WW Russian/Ukrainian speaking community manager - she spearheaded those efforts to fix/avoid stuff like Baba Yaga and WW agreed. You can find her youtube channel, twitter and vk.com (post-Soviet fb) - she's an admin of the Vampire:The Masquerade group there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T07:28:28-08:00","id":1425511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425505#post1425505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I like the way you think, I wonder how many city's would have the Tremere locked in their house scared to come out and be eaten by a resurgent Clan Salubri. HokusPokus wont stop a broadsword from removing your head as you make your way to the local Elysium gathering. Political power means little to Sabbat rules of warfare, or lack there of.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Probably not that many. The Tremere beat the Salubri back when the Salubri were an established clan, and the Tremere were universally reviled and hobbled at near every turn by those around them. The Tremere have better logistics for a war, and if the Salubri upped their scale they'd gain the ire of everyone who would've supported them. Even in the -FUCK TREMERE- environment of V5, it'd be a stretch to imagine the Salubri regularly winning any engagements they'd make. Though I suppose a sense of internal realism comes secondary to a plot full of juicy scandal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T07:56:45-08:00","id":1425517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425511#post1425511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Probably not that many. The Tremere beat the Salubri back when the Salubri were an established clan, and the Tremere were universally reviled and hobbled at near every turn by those around them. The Tremere have better logistics for a war, and if the Salubri upped their scale they'd gain the ire of everyone who would've supported them. Even in the -FUCK TREMERE- environment of V5, it'd be a stretch to imagine the Salubri regularly winning any engagements they'd make. Though I suppose a sense of internal realism comes secondary to a plot full of juicy scandal.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But are they not a broken fractured Clan themselves now? If the Council was destroyed or at the very least taken off the board and different factions are vying for power they seem to be as broken as the Salubri were with the healers and warriors getting divorced. Young Tremere don't have much to defend themselves from armed extremists and less of a power structure to fall back on. I think the odds have evened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T07:59:07-08:00","id":1425518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425509#post1425509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You can reach out for comment to Natalie Manzurenko, the WW Russian/Ukrainian speaking community manager - she spearheaded those efforts to fix/avoid stuff like Baba Yaga and WW agreed. You can find her youtube channel, twitter and vk.com (post-Soviet fb) - she's an admin of the Vampire:The Masquerade group there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll be sure to do so after I get with the person from Egypt who wants to stop WW and the rest of the world from using Set so inappropriately.<br /> <br /> I should add both need to wait for me to talk with the various clergy, since I promise you fa far far more Christians are offended by VTM wrapping blood sucking murderers up with their God, Jesus (Knights of the Bitter Ash, Grail Covenant, ETC...), the land of Nod, CAINE, Etc...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","user":"Vamps Like Us","date":". 11-22-2020, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T08:16:31-08:00","id":1425520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425518#post1425518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'll be sure to do so after I get with the person from Egypt who wants to stop WW and the rest of the world from using Set so inappropriately.<br /> <br /> I should add both need to wait for me to talk with the various clergy, since I promise you fa far far more Christians are offended by VTM wrapping blood sucking murderers up with their God, Jesus (Knights of the Bitter Ash, Grail Covenant, ETC...), the land of Nod, CAINE, Etc...</div> </div> </div> </div>So you confirmed your argument about 'asserting on the internet only' was nonsense.<br /> <br /> Unless you are Mark Rein Hagen or Justin Achilli or Jason Carl or any other WW big gun, I am not interested in such a discussion. Something tells me no one among them at WW would even conceive arguments like yours let alone allow such an attitude into their future books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","user":"Val_Nir","date":". 11-22-2020, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T08:17:31-08:00","id":1425522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tremere have better logistics for a war</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, the Tremere have been screwed over this edition both in-verse and meta-wise. They're practically done as a Clan already. It doesn't even NEED to be the Salubri that re-upstage the Tremere out of influence, the Assamites being keyed into the Camarilla and taking over the Tremere's role soft-power wise by the writers is the knoll on their doorstep already. To boot this is the most fractious the Tremere has ever been and now they can be blood-bonded more easier by ANYONE and like mentioned before, the Council is out the window. The Tremere are finished by how they were handled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T10:38:00-08:00","id":1425538,"title":"","content":"THE TREMERE WILL RISE AGAIN, JUST AS THE SABBAT SHALL RETURN TO SWALLOW THE ANARCHS, AND SET'S CHILDREN WILL BECOME HIS FOLLOWERS ONCE MORE, AND ALSO WE'LL BE ABLE TO DOMINATE INFORMATION OUT OF PEOPLE AGAIN.... <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/ef/57/d6/ef57d6e296ca46b6c8e2cf055cf4b56a.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Seriously though. If it weren't for meta-bullshit, the Tremere would absolutely shred if push came to shove. Omen war 2 would be an excellent Gehenna conflict, even if it were Tremere VS everyone else. The Tremere have all sorts of exciting cards to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T17:08:20-08:00","id":1425587,"title":"","content":"Having the Tremere vs the Rest would actually make an interesting premise for a Chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T17:43:16-08:00","id":1425591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425518#post1425518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'll be sure to do so after I get with the person from Egypt who wants to stop WW and the rest of the world from using Set so inappropriately.<br /> <br /> I should add both need to wait for me to talk with the various clergy, since I promise you fa far far more Christians are offended by VTM wrapping blood sucking murderers up with their God, Jesus (Knights of the Bitter Ash, Grail Covenant, ETC...), the land of Nod, CAINE, Etc...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is nonsense. Everyone doesn't have to be on the same page for some people to take issue with how their folklore is represented.<br /> <br /> Plus the difference in the case of Christianity is that Jesus is not literally depicted with a character sheet as a bloodsucking fiend of the night, and the beliefs in him as a vampire are clearly marked as heresies.<br /> <br /> But also, you're shifting the goalposts and that's just rude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T18:39:35-08:00","id":1425599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425591#post1425591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is nonsense. Everyone doesn't have to be on the same page for some people to take issue with how their folklore is represented.<br /> <br /> Plus the difference in the case of Christianity is that Jesus is not literally depicted with a character sheet as a bloodsucking fiend of the night, and the beliefs in him as a vampire are clearly marked as heresies.<br /> <br /> But also, you're shifting the goalposts and that's just rude.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No not really I just don't take it seriously as wide spread. A mythical creature (Baba Yaga) was turned into a different mythical creature (a Nosfuratu vampire) and did mean things. That is far less offensive than say Al Capone who could very easily have killed a relative of someone alive in the 90s playing the game is more offensive than Baba Yaga. <br /> <br /> I'm Greek (by way of America) and I say Helen of Troy, part of my historical culture weather or not she was really real was a victim and portraying her as a monster who rules Chicago with a bloody fist is offensive to me as a Greek American. Do you agree we should get rid of Helena? Why not if I say it's offensive. Or is VTM a game and if i tiny amount of people are offended they can say not in my world. Forgive me if I find it hard to sympathise with the treatment of a fairy tale. Where do you draw the line while making a game in &quot;Our world only darker&quot;?<br /> <br /> Gypsy and Ravnos were offensive stereotypes of real people, the current real life tragedy that was used for story fodder was a terrible and insensitive idea, People follow Christianity and are offended by VTM I've met some yet no one seems to care(and din't hte Knights drink from Christ and get super powers where they don't drink, wasn't the cup of Christ the point of 3 novels, and Cain has no stats, is he then somehow not part of the game for lacking a character sheet?). Baba Yaga is wait for it...Make Believe. So Baba Yaga was offensive to the point of killing her off? fine she's dead in cannon, and as I see it as a bad call, alive and well in mine.<br /> <br /> I find Baba Yaga as a great offence so off, when Val Nir said he didn't want to talk about it with me I was happy to drop it. Now I will say this is so silly to me I don't see the point of talking about it so wont bother to respond to the offended that may quote me.<br /> <br /> Baba Yaga...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T18:45:12-08:00","id":1425601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425599#post1425599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No not really I just don't take it seriously as wide spread. A mythical creature (Baba Yaga) was turned into a different mythical creature (a Nosfuratu vampire) and did mean things. That is far less offensive than say Al Capone who could very easily have killed a relative of someone alive in the 90s playing the game is more offensive than Baba Yaga.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about you or what you think, it's about the people who actually had something to say about it. Other people complaining or not complaining about other issues in the WoD doesn't lend or remove validity to this particular complaint.<br /> <br /> A lot of Romany people objected heavily to the WoD book purportedly about their culture as well as the Ravnos depictions in second edition. People objected to other portrayals in the WoD. White Wolf responded accordingly to these complaints, and phantom complaints you introduce here that didn't happen have no bearing or relevance on real world events.<br /> <br /> I'm not offended by your remarks, I just think you're extremely off base to make comparisons like this to cast doubt on real world events.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T18:55:07-08:00","id":1425603,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Dial it down please. Everyone should note that players have the right to be offended by portrayals and share those feelings. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T19:25:31-08:00","id":1425608,"title":"","content":"lots of false equivolence here: <br /> with Caine, He was written from the perspective of someone who knows the story, and the story was twisted appropriately, but also <br /> Other good examples include Fenrir and Set: people who know the mythology gave new perspectives. Or at least they gave good ideas by revised. <br /> <br /> with gypsies, someone clearly doesn't know the story. and just wants to get nasty. <br /> with Baba Yaga, someone just didnt understand it was a kids story and it just seems silly, maybe more than a little patronizing. <br /> <br /> There seems to be this idiotic idea that punching a well established group (christianity) is good while punching a fringe group is always bad. That's a pretty hairy idea when one group you consider 'punching up' because it's a majority somewhere or because you feel it's 'wrong and dangerous' feels it's a category that gets punched down on routinely (Eastern europeans, russians especially, or 'rednecks') <br /> <br /> Really, so long as you understand what others believe in and can apply creative liscence alt-histories in a way that seems like a natural part of the setting, rather than as an agenda push, you can punch who you like.<br /> <br /> edit:<br /> aw phipps. This is what happens when I post on a phone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 11-22-2020, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T19:59:50-08:00","id":1425617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425603#post1425603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Dial it down please. Everyone should note that players have the right to be offended by portrayals and share those feelings. </span></div> </div> </div> </div>Al Capone who really could have murdered a father or other family member in real life of a person or even a family playing the game in 1991 would be a far more legit argument of being offended and it would still be stupid to kill off Al Capone, because everyone I knew and most people in general I'll bet thought Capone being one of Lodin's Childer was cool, Untouchables was a big hit at the time.<br /> <br /> Yes, some vocal people were offended by Baba Yaga. They killed her off, and the game is worse for it, B.Y. is cool. In the last decade small minorities of people making lot's of noise have gotten lots of changes to lots of things that most people liked or were not bothered by, common sense is required sometimes too. Where is the line drawn in a game based on our actual history and places and yes myths and folk lore. Of course some things were right to be corrected (Ravnos), this was not one of them and the game gets more milquetoast.<br /> <br /> Helen of Troy vs King Menelaous, Al Capone, Baba Yaga, Robin Hood, Set, even Louis Pasture showing his face gives the game flavor. I'm quite confident Baba Yaga was popular over all, it's why she is used in movies books comic books and so on, and if you make a game that is very popular with all these flavor bits, and then start taking them away for fear of offending a small vocal minority, you get a blander game.<br /> <br /> Of course people can be offended and say so, it does not however automatically make it a wide spread problem that needs correcting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","user":"Vamps Like Us","date":". 11-22-2020, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T20:31:36-08:00","id":1425625,"title":"","content":"Getting back to the topic of Modiphius being replaced by Renegade Studios as the publishers of V5:<br /> <br /> I'm of two minds. On one hand, I'm curious as to why Modiphius is dropped. The second, I'm a little leery that a company that I've never heard of before the announcement of the V5 Players' Companion is going to be the defacto publisher of the ttrpg. Forgive me, but I don't play ccg card games. I played Jyhad back in the '90s before the brand name switch to VTES, so, a card game company is going to publish my favorite rpg... Call me skeptical, but I think that V5 will be too much to handle for them.....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">R<i>emember, remember, the Fifth of November, the Gunpowder Treason and Plot. I know of no reason why the Gunpowder Treason should ever be forgot.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> -V for Vendetta</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/997-japheth","name":"Japheth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar997_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T21:37:28-08:00","id":1425636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Japheth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425625#post1425625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getting back to the topic of Modiphius being replaced by Renegade Studios as the publishers of V5:<br /> <br /> I'm of two minds. On one hand, I'm curious as to why Modiphius is dropped. The second, I'm a little leery that a company that I've never heard of before the announcement of the V5 Players' Companion is going to be the defacto publisher of the ttrpg. Forgive me, but I don't play ccg card games. I played Jyhad back in the '90s before the brand name switch to VTES, so, a card game company is going to publish my favorite rpg... Call me skeptical, but I think that V5 will be too much to handle for them.....</div> </div> </div> </div>They do RPGs as well as card games, tabletop games, and other products. It's not a one trick publisher.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T21:44:14-08:00","id":1425639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Japheth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425625#post1425625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getting back to the topic of Modiphius being replaced by Renegade Studios as the publishers of V5:<br /> <br /> I'm of two minds. On one hand, I'm curious as to why Modiphius is dropped. The second, I'm a little leery that a company that I've never heard of before the announcement of the V5 Players' Companion is going to be the defacto publisher of the ttrpg. Forgive me, but I don't play ccg card games. I played Jyhad back in the '90s before the brand name switch to VTES, so, a card game company is going to publish my favorite rpg... Call me skeptical, but I think that V5 will be too much to handle for them.....</div> </div> </div> </div>It may just be that Modiphius only decided to take on the license to ensure it kept going, but didn\u2019t really have the passion to make it a lasting line. They certainly sold a lot of the core-book from retail figures, which would justify why they would choose to initially take it on, but actually Onyx Path is overtaking them a lot in terms of support. There may have also been lots of editing issues behind the scenes that made them think again too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T21:45:32-08:00","id":1425640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425636#post1425636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They do RPGs as well as card games, tabletop games, and other products. It's not a one trick publisher.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What rpgs? I only saw the card game on their site. I even looked at their product lists, and I've never heard of any of their games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">R<i>emember, remember, the Fifth of November, the Gunpowder Treason and Plot. I know of no reason why the Gunpowder Treason should ever be forgot.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> -V for Vendetta</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/997-japheth","name":"Japheth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar997_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T21:49:31-08:00","id":1425643,"title":"","content":"Multiple RPGs listed on this page. They're just not grouped together. Also several on that page are not marked as RPGs, but in fact are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.renegadegamestudios.com/games\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://cdn11.bigcommerce.com/s-kftzvkkgjv/product_images/uploaded_images/rgs.fb.discord.1200x627-2022.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.renegadegamestudios.com/games\" target=\"_blank\"> Renegade Game Studios - Not Found </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.renegadegamestudios.com/games\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.renegadegamestudios.com/games </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Renegade Games Online Store </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T22:03:24-08:00","id":1425648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425643#post1425643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Multiple RPGs listed on this page. They're just not grouped together. Also several on that page are not marked as RPGs, but in fact are.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.renegadegamestudios.com/games\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.renegadegamestudios.com/games</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> All I saw was mini-niche games that, as I said, I've never heard of. The only major name in that list was Power Rangers that I wouldn't be interested in at all. All other products are just.....meh.<br /> <br /> I don't think that they'll be able to handle it.<br /> <br /> P.S... If White Wolf Entertainment makes an announcement that OPP still will be involved in publishing WoD material, it will be a relief... I trust OPP far more than RGS.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">R<i>emember, remember, the Fifth of November, the Gunpowder Treason and Plot. I know of no reason why the Gunpowder Treason should ever be forgot.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> -V for Vendetta</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/997-japheth","name":"Japheth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar997_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T22:04:32-08:00","id":1425650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Japheth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425640#post1425640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What rpgs? I only saw the card game on their site. I even looked at their product lists, and I've never heard of any of their games.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The rpgs are published through their arrangement with Hunters Entertainment, Renegade itself hasn't done any RPGs. However they do share some people who have worked on some of Hunters rpgs.<br /> <br /> Of those Outbreak Undead and Altered Carbon are......not good. Alice is missing is gimmicky but good for what it is. And Kids on Bikes/Brooms is a tad derivative but solid.<br /> <br /> So not a great track record and certainly not very experienced and a number of the staff have recently moved on to other things......so who knows how it will shake out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T22:05:48-08:00","id":1425651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1423253-modiphius-is-bo-longer-the-publisher-of-vtm-renegade-studios-is?p=1425617#post1425617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Al Capone who really could have murdered a father or other family member in real life of a person or even a family playing the game in 1991 would be a far more legit argument of being offended and it would still be stupid to kill off Al Capone, because everyone I knew and most people in general I'll bet thought Capone being one of Lodin's Childer was cool, Untouchables was a big hit at the time.<br /> <br /> Yes, some vocal people were offended by Baba Yaga. They killed her off, and the game is worse for it, B.Y. is cool. In the last decade small minorities of people making lot's of noise have gotten lots of changes to lots of things that most people liked or were not bothered by, common sense is required sometimes too. Where is the line drawn in a game based on our actual history and places and yes myths and folk lore. Of course some things were right to be corrected (Ravnos), this was not one of them and the game gets more milquetoast.<br /> <br /> Helen of Troy vs King Menelaous, Al Capone, Baba Yaga, Robin Hood, Set, even Louis Pasture showing his face gives the game flavor. I'm quite confident Baba Yaga was popular over all, it's why she is used in movies books comic books and so on, and if you make a game that is very popular with all these flavor bits, and then start taking them away for fear of offending a small vocal minority, you get a blander game.<br /> <br /> Of course people can be offended and say so, it does not however automatically make it a wide spread problem that needs correcting.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Please leave the thread. When I make a statement in red, I do not do it to be argued with or discussed. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i>